{
  "Uuid": "4fdbf1e4-5845-484e-8d84-5ec4fec16069",
  "IsCustomNode": false,
  "Description": "",
  "Name": "Home",
  "ElementResolver": {
    "ResolutionMap": {}
  },
  "Inputs": [],
  "Outputs": [],
  "Nodes": [
    {
      "ConcreteType": "PythonNodeModels.PythonNode, PythonNodeModels",
      "Code": "# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\r\n\"\"\"Revit Dynamo CPython3 — v6.18.2 ORIGINAL MARKERS + ELEVATION LEFT HIDDEN X CUT HEIGHT.\r\n\r\nStart from a CLEAN ORIGINAL SHEET in a disposable/backup project.\r\nRestores 1:25-first fitting with a second content-aware layout solver when the\r\noriginal section markers inflate Revit viewport crop/bounding boxes. Now also\r\nrepositions ORIGINAL section markers closer to Plan Detail geometry and attempts\r\nto shorten their view crop width without losing visible source model geometry. Keeps\r\ntwo-row geometry-aligned layout, BOM/checklist/notes collision checking, and\r\ndynamic marker discovery.\r\n\r\nNEW DEFAULT: Mirror the EXISTING Elevation Front section marker once, using the\r\nproven bbox-center mirror test. Do not create replacement sections, hide\r\noriginals, or mirror Elevation Left by default. The source Elevation view's \r\nOrigin and CropBox CAN CHANGE; the script reports this as a known side effect. \r\n\r\nAfter mirroring, horizontally re-align Elevation Front and Elevation Left\r\nviewport titles to the actually projected model geometry; Plan Detail title\r\ncontinues to use the tested v6.13 geometry-based anchor. Reapply this alignment\r\nAFTER viewport placement, so the layout solver doesn't undo the title fix.\r\n\r\nIN[0]: ViewSheet or None for active Revit sheet.\r\nIN[1]: optional Python dictionary; e.g. {'force_scale':25}.\r\nIN[2]: True / None (DEFAULT) = trial transactions only; False = COMMIT.\r\n\r\nUse {'skip_original_mirror':True} ONLY for a sheet whose original section\r\nwas ALREADY mirrored once. Running default twice can reverse the original\r\nmarker mirror and modify the source Elevation again. This script does not\r\nedit section marker's blue endpoint grips directly. The optional crop-width\r\ntrim is an EXPERIMENT: Revit may link the displayed section line length to the\r\nsource ViewSection.CropBox, which also changes real source-view contents.\r\nEvery candidate is verified and rolled back unless IN[2]=False.\r\n\"\"\"\r\nimport clr\r\nimport math\r\nclr.AddReference('RevitAPI')\r\nclr.AddReference('RevitServices')\r\nfrom Autodesk.Revit.DB import (\r\n    ViewSheet, ViewSection, ViewType, Viewport, ElementId, XYZ, AssemblyInstance,\r\n    Transaction, TransactionGroup, SubTransaction, TransactionStatus, FilteredElementCollector,\r\n    TextNote, ScheduleSheetInstance, FamilyInstance, BuiltInCategory, CategoryType,\r\n    Plane, ElementTransformUtils, ReferenceableViewUtils\r\n)\r\nfrom RevitServices.Persistence import DocumentManager\r\nfrom RevitServices.Transactions import TransactionManager\r\nfrom System.Collections.Generic import List\r\nfrom System import Convert\r\n\r\nDOC = DocumentManager.Instance.CurrentDBDocument\r\nFT_TO_MM = 304.8\r\n\r\nDEFAULTS = {\r\n    # None means process the ACTIVE/EXPLICITLY PASSED ViewSheet, not an old\r\n    # hard-coded sheet number. For a batch or safety lock, provide an override:\r\n    # {'expected_sheet_number':'ATSYD3-B310-HL-RR01-TCSF-292'}\r\n    'expected_sheet_number': None,\r\n    # Only for the original example's fixed BOM fallback. Other sheets must\r\n    # detect BOM header dynamically or supply bom_header_left_override_mm.\r\n    'sample_sheet_number_for_bom_fallback': 'ATSYD3-B320-LL-RR07-18-TCSF-2344',\r\n    'marker_strategy': 'original_direct_mirror',  # or 'reference_recreation_v613'\r\n    'mirror_original_front': True,\r\n    'mirror_original_left': False,\r\n    'skip_original_mirror': False,  # set True on an already-mirrored ORIGINAL sheet\r\n    # v6.17: bring the REAL section lines next to the Plan Detail model.\r\n    # Moving an original marker also moves its real section cut plane; this is\r\n    # NOT a schematic-only translation. It can change Elevation source views.\r\n    'original_marker_proximity': True,\r\n    'original_marker_vertical_gap_mm': 8.0,    # line 3 LEFT of model\r\n    'original_marker_horizontal_gap_mm': 8.0,  # line 4 BELOW model\r\n    'original_marker_max_move_mm': 165.0,     # per-axis cap on paper\r\n    'original_marker_position_tolerance_mm': 0.65,\r\n    # Try reducing the REAL section view's crop width, which often shortens the\r\n    # line displayed in the parent Plan. It cannot be guaranteed by the API.\r\n    'original_marker_try_crop_trim': True,\r\n    'original_marker_crop_padding_mm': 5.0,\r\n    'original_marker_min_crop_width_mm': 20.0,\r\n    'original_marker_crop_max_shrink_fraction': 0.90,\r\n    # Fail rather than silently changing which visible MODEL elements are seen\r\n    # in the source Elevation views. Note this is not a pixel-equivalence test.\r\n    'original_marker_require_source_model_ids_unchanged': True,\r\n    'original_marker_require_source_annotations_unchanged': True,\r\n    'original_marker_warn_if_envelope_not_reduced': True,\r\n    # v6.18.2: Find the original Plan Detail (often labelled X) section marker\r\n    # HIDDEN in Elevation Left, move its cutting plane ABOVE the full assembly.\r\n    # The plan is expected to face DOWN in the Elevation Left view.\r\n    'elevation_left_hidden_x_to_top': True,\r\n    'elevation_left_hidden_x_names': ['Plan Detail', 'X'],\r\n    'elevation_left_hidden_x_gap_mm': 30.0,      # approx. expected.png: line ~30mm above assembly top\r\n    'elevation_left_hidden_x_max_move_mm': 180.0,\r\n    'elevation_left_hidden_x_tolerance_mm': 0.8,\r\n    'elevation_left_hidden_x_min_facing_dot': 0.65, # diagnostic only; not a view-head test\r\n    'elevation_left_hidden_x_allow_plan_origin_fallback': True,\r\n    'elevation_left_hidden_x_require_all_members_visible': False,\r\n    # If target cannot be uniquely identified, do NOT guess; leave marker alone\r\n    # and report candidate IDs in 'elevation_left_x_preflight'. Layout continues.\r\n    'elevation_left_hidden_x_missing_policy': 'error', # 'skip' to explicitly allow non-X sheets\r\n    'original_marker_title_alignment': True,\r\n    'align_elevation_titles_to_model': ['front','left'],\r\n    'label_left_of_model_mm': 2.0,\r\n    'max_geometry_title_shift_mm': 120.0,\r\n    'geometry_title_tolerance_mm': 1.25,\r\n    'plan_name': 'Plan Detail',\r\n    'front_name': 'Elevation Front',\r\n    'left_name': 'Elevation Left',\r\n    'iso_name': '3D Ortho',\r\n    # Legacy marker/view IDs are hints only; the actual elements are resolved\r\n    # from placed sheet views and visible markers in Plan Detail.\r\n    'references': [\r\n        {'name':'Elevation Left', 'view_id':2042332, 'marker_id':2042331,\r\n         'axis':'vertical', 'head_end':'positive'},\r\n        {'name':'Elevation Front', 'view_id':2042341, 'marker_id':2042340,\r\n         'axis':'horizontal', 'head_end':'negative'},\r\n    ],\r\n    # V6.9: create front with head left (correct facing), then MIRROR around\r\n    # the shared tail so head finishes right WITHOUT shifting the tail.\r\n    'mirror_front_reference_about_tail': True,\r\n    # v6.13: Reference-section markers are ANNOTATIONS referencing existing\r\n    # Detail views. The default proximity mode draws the L beside the measured\r\n    # Plan Detail model, instead of at the source view cut-plane intersection.\r\n    # The underlying source Detail views, their origin, and their crop stay intact.\r\n    'marker_placement_mode': 'geometry_proximity', # or 'source_cut_plane'\r\n    'vertical_marker_clearance_from_geometry_mm': 8.0,   # line 3 left of model\r\n    'horizontal_marker_clearance_from_geometry_mm': 8.0, # line 4 below model\r\n    'max_marker_move_from_source_mm': 165.0,  # sanity limit, paper millimetres\r\n    'require_schematic_marker_confirmation': False, # opt-in available for stricter policies\r\n    # Short parts require shorter markers than 1:50 pipe runs. Still cover model.\r\n\r\n    'shared_tail_cut_plane_tolerance_mm': 1.0,  # allowed model-to-paper difference\r\n    'vertical_height_ratios': [1.0, 0.95, 0.90],\r\n    # Full-geometry marker coverage (all lengths in paper millimetres). Both\r\n    # section reference CUT PLANES remain unchanged; only line endpoints extend.\r\n    'horizontal_cover_all_plan_geometry': True,\r\n    'horizontal_geometry_margin_mm': 3.0,\r\n    'vertical_geometry_margin_mm': 4.0,\r\n    'horizontal_tail_stub_mm': 5.0,  # extension LEFT of shared line intersection\r\n    'vertical_tail_stub_mm': 5.0,    # extension BELOW shared line intersection\r\n    'marker_max_length_paper_mm': 275.0, # fail if required coverage exceeds this\r\n    # 1:25 is attempted FIRST; it is not a hard rule. 1:50 is a fallback ONLY\r\n    # after strict and content-aware 1:25 placement BOTH fail.\r\n    'scale_selection_mode': 'largest_fit', # try 1:25 then 1:50, 1:75, 1:100\r\n    'scale_candidates': [25, 50, 75, 100],\r\n    # Original markers can enlarge viewport crop outlines unrelated to drawn\r\n    # content. For 1:25 only, retry using the ACTUAL projected drawing content\r\n    # (model + visible annotation/reference-marker graphics + viewport titles).\r\n    # Never ignore the marker graphics, BOM, checklist, or notes in this mode.\r\n    'enable_25_content_footprints': True,\r\n    'content_geometry_clearance_mm': 2.0,\r\n    # v6.16: L-shaped original markers are treated as SEPARATE printed parts.\r\n    # The previous two-row max-height sum overestimated 1:25 requirements.\r\n    # This solver permits row bounding-box intersections ONLY when actual\r\n    # model, annotation, title parts are all mutually collision-free.\r\n    'enable_25_sparse_parts': True,\r\n    'sparse_printed_sheet_margin_mm': 2.0,\r\n    'sparse_candidate_samples': 9,\r\n    'sparse_secondary_samples': 7,\r\n    'sparse_max_view_parts': 80,\r\n    'sparse_max_search_trials': 65000,\r\n\r\n    'content_max_annotation_candidates': 450,\r\n    # If the content projection fails, do not guess from incomplete bounds.\r\n    'fail_on_missing_view_content': True,\r\n\r\n    'force_scale': None, # optional override, e.g. 25, still must pass layout\r\n    'vertical_top_and_bottom_margin_mm': 4.0,\r\n    'vertical_min_length_paper_mm': 22.0,\r\n    'horizontal_length_paper_mm': 20.0,  # minimum, length grows to cover geometry\r\n    'require_matching_source_facing': True,  # initial creation always uses the known upward-facing geometry\r\n    'allow_reversed_horizontal_preview': False,\r\n    'approve_reversed_horizontal_commit': False,\r\n\r\n    # V6: use BOM HEADER x; set override in IN[1] if Revit BOM not detected.\r\n    'bom_header_left_override_mm': None,  # mm from sheet's left; optional\r\n    'bom_header_detection_names': ['Mark','Size','Qty','Description'],\r\n    'bom_clearance_mm': 10.0,\r\n    'bom_keepout_top_band_mm': 80.0,  # protects upper-right sheet region\r\n    'geometry_alignment_tolerance_mm': 0.75,\r\n    'require_geometry_alignment': True,\r\n    'preferred_scale': 50,  # reporting preference only; not a hard requirement\r\n    'fallback_scales': [25, 75, 100],\r\n    'allow_fallback_commit': True,\r\n    'require_preferred_scale_for_sample_sheet': False,\r\n    'min_height_saving_paper_mm': 0.0,   # reject marker replacement that increases plan height\r\n    'max_marker_profiles': 18,          # cap geometry ratio/title-gap previews\r\n\r\n    'cut_line_tolerance_paper_mm': 20.0, # verify source cut plane near old marker bbox\r\n    'min_model_element_count': 1,\r\n    'gap_mm': 12.0,                  # between drawing regions\r\n    'minimum_gap_mm': 5.0,\r\n    'obstacle_clearance_mm': 2.0,\r\n    'sheet_margin_mm': 8.0,\r\n    'label_gap_mm': 5.0,              # default title offset; dynamically tested at 1:50\r\n    'search_label_gap_mm': [5.0,3.0,2.0],  # title-to-viewport clearances; avoid <2mm by default\r\n    'label_line_mm': 40.0,\r\n    'post_replacement_title_reanchor': True,  # fix stranded titles after section bounds shrink\r\n    'plan_title_anchor_to_geometry': True,\r\n    'title_align_mode_plan': 'geometry_left',\r\n    'plan_title_from_geometry_offset_mm': -3.0,\r\n    'title_label_max_height_mm': 45.0,  # abort on implausible View Title families\r\n    'title_reanchor_tolerance_mm': 1.5,\r\n    'reserved_right_fraction': 0.235,    # titleblock BOM and checklist family\r\n    'reserved_bottom_fraction': 0.115,   # first-pass conservative notes reserve\r\n    # Retry 1:25 with a smaller conservative FOOTER reserve; fixed note and\r\n    # legend keepouts and the printed-page title check are still enforced.\r\n    'allow_compact_footer_retry_at_25': True,\r\n    'compact_footer_fraction_at_25': 0.075,\r\n    'keepouts_normalized': [],\r\n    'elastic_samples': 17,\r\n    # v6.10: anchored visual template, from user-provided 1-result.png.\r\n    # Fractions use [left-to-right X, bottom-to-top Y] of full paper sheet.\r\n    # The targets describe projected MODEL center, not the oversized viewport\r\n    # bounding box center, and are adjusted as needed for real collisions.\r\n    'layout_mode': 'reference_1_result',   # or 'legacy_balanced'\r\n    # v6.13: based on uploaded 1-expected(1).png; model centroids, not viewports.\r\n    # Coordinates are [fraction of sheet width from left,\r\n    #                  fraction of sheet height from BOTTOM].\r\n    # Front and Plan deliberately share one X goal to preserve their alignment.\r\n    'layout_model_center_targets': {\r\n        'front': [0.23, 0.76],\r\n        'left':  [0.50, 0.76],\r\n        'plan':  [0.23, 0.34],\r\n        'iso':   [0.57, 0.34],\r\n    },\r\n    'layout_target_weights': {'front': 3.0, 'left': 2.0,\r\n                              'plan': 3.0, 'iso': 1.8},\r\n    'layout_target_candidate_rows': 15,\r\n    'title_page_clearance_mm': 2.0,\r\n    'max_reference_center_error_mm': 50.0, # refuse to commit a layout too far from 1-result\r\n    'hide_markers_outside_plan': True,  # only markers with placed-view names\r\n    'approve_marker_orientation': False,\r\n    'approve_commit': False,\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef mm_to_ft(value): return float(value) / FT_TO_MM\r\n\r\ndef elem_num(obj):\r\n    identifier = getattr(obj,'Id',obj)\r\n    try: return int(identifier.Value)\r\n    except Exception:\r\n        try: return int(identifier.IntegerValue)\r\n        except Exception: return str(identifier)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef eid(n): return ElementId(int(n))\r\n\r\ndef enum_num(v): return int(Convert.ToInt32(v))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef vec(p): return [p.X,p.Y,p.Z]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef xyz_info(p): return [round(p.X,4), round(p.Y,4),round(p.Z,4)]\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Rect:\r\n    def __init__(self, x0,y0,x1,y1):\r\n        self.x0=float(min(x0,x1)); self.x1=float(max(x0,x1))\r\n        self.y0=float(min(y0,y1)); self.y1=float(max(y0,y1))\r\n    @property\r\n    def w(self):return self.x1-self.x0\r\n    @property\r\n    def h(self):return self.y1-self.y0\r\n    @property\r\n    def cx(self):return (self.x0+self.x1)/2.0\r\n    @property\r\n    def cy(self):return (self.y0+self.y1)/2.0\r\n    def move(self,dx,dy):return Rect(self.x0+dx,self.y0+dy,self.x1+dx,self.y1+dy)\r\n    def expand(self,a):return Rect(self.x0-a,self.y0-a,self.x1+a,self.y1+a)\r\n    def overlaps(self,other,eps=0):\r\n        return (self.x0<other.x1-eps and self.x1>other.x0+eps and\r\n                self.y0<other.y1-eps and self.y1>other.y0+eps)\r\n    def fits(self,other,eps=1e-7):\r\n        return (self.x0>=other.x0-eps and self.x1<=other.x1+eps and\r\n                self.y0>=other.y0-eps and self.y1<=other.y1+eps)\r\n    def as_mm(self):return [round(v*FT_TO_MM,2) for v in (self.x0,self.y0,self.x1,self.y1)]\r\n    def size_mm(self):return [round(self.w*FT_TO_MM,2),round(self.h*FT_TO_MM,2)]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef raw_outline(outline):\r\n    if outline is None:return None\r\n    a=outline.MinimumPoint;b=outline.MaximumPoint\r\n    values=(a.X,a.Y,b.X,b.Y)\r\n    # Empty label outlines sometimes use reversed enormous Revit sentinels.\r\n    if any(not math.isfinite(x) or abs(x)>10000 for x in values):return None\r\n    if a.X>=b.X or a.Y>=b.Y:return None\r\n    return Rect(a.X,a.Y,b.X,b.Y)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef viewport_box(vp):\r\n    box=raw_outline(vp.GetBoxOutline())\r\n    if box is None:raise ValueError('Invalid viewport box: '+str(elem_num(vp)))\r\n    return box\r\n\r\n\r\ndef viewport_footprint(vp):\r\n    box=viewport_box(vp)\r\n    try:label=raw_outline(vp.GetLabelOutline())\r\n    except Exception:label=None\r\n    if label is None:return box\r\n    return Rect(min(box.x0,label.x0),min(box.y0,label.y0),\r\n                max(box.x1,label.x1),max(box.y1,label.y1))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef bounds_from_bb(bb, basis_view):\r\n    if bb is None:return None\r\n    try:\r\n        # BoundingBoxXYZ's Min/Max are in its Transform local coordinates.\r\n        transform=bb.Transform\r\n        corners=[]\r\n        for x in (bb.Min.X,bb.Max.X):\r\n            for y in (bb.Min.Y,bb.Max.Y):\r\n                for z in (bb.Min.Z,bb.Max.Z):\r\n                    p=transform.OfPoint(XYZ(x,y,z)).Subtract(basis_view.Origin)\r\n                    corners.append((p.DotProduct(basis_view.RightDirection),\r\n                                    p.DotProduct(basis_view.UpDirection)))\r\n        return Rect(min(p[0] for p in corners), min(p[1] for p in corners),\r\n                    max(p[0] for p in corners), max(p[1] for p in corners))\r\n    except Exception:return None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef find_sheet_view(sheet,name):\r\n    hits=[]\r\n    for vp_id in sheet.GetAllViewports():\r\n        vp=DOC.GetElement(vp_id)\r\n        view=DOC.GetElement(vp.ViewId)\r\n        if view is not None and str(view.Name).strip().lower()==str(name).strip().lower():\r\n            hits.append((vp,view))\r\n    if len(hits)!=1:\r\n        raise ValueError('Expected one placed view named %r; found %d'%(name,len(hits)))\r\n    return hits[0]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef get_targets(sheet,cfg):\r\n    target={}\r\n    for key,name in [('plan',cfg['plan_name']),('front',cfg['front_name']),\r\n                     ('left',cfg['left_name']),('iso',cfg['iso_name'])]:\r\n        target[key]=find_sheet_view(sheet,name)\r\n    return target\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _marker_categories():\r\n    cats=set()\r\n    for builtin_name in ('OST_Viewers','OST_Sections','OST_ReferenceViewer'):\r\n        try:cats.add(enum_num(getattr(BuiltInCategory,builtin_name)))\r\n        except Exception:pass\r\n    return cats\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _candidate_marker_info(element,plan):\r\n    out={'id':elem_num(element),'name':str(element.Name),\r\n         'element_class':element.GetType().Name}\r\n    try:out['category']=str(element.Category.Name) if element.Category else None\r\n    except Exception:out['category']=None\r\n    try:out['hidden']=bool(element.IsHidden(plan))\r\n    except Exception:out['hidden']=None\r\n    try:out['can_hide']=bool(element.CanBeHidden(plan))\r\n    except Exception:out['can_hide']=False\r\n    try:\r\n        b=bounds_from_bb(element.get_BoundingBox(plan),plan)\r\n        out['bbox_in_plan_ft']=None if b is None else [\r\n            round(b.x0,4),round(b.y0,4),round(b.x1,4),round(b.y1,4)]\r\n    except Exception:out['bbox_in_plan_ft']=None\r\n    try:out['linked_view_id']=elem_num(ReferenceableViewUtils.GetReferencedViewId(DOC,element.Id))\r\n    except Exception:out['linked_view_id']=None\r\n    return out\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _is_marker_candidate(element,plan,source_name,cats):\r\n    # These are the annotation/viewer marker instances, NOT the source Detail view.\r\n    try:\r\n        if str(element.Name).strip().lower()!=str(source_name).strip().lower():return False\r\n        if isinstance(element,ViewSection):return False\r\n        category=element.Category\r\n        if category is None:return False\r\n        catid=elem_num(category.Id)\r\n        cat_name=str(category.Name).strip().lower()\r\n        if catid not in cats and cat_name not in ('views','sections','reference viewer','reference viewers'):\r\n            return False\r\n        # Require a view-specific bounding box to avoid finding elements on other sheets.\r\n        if bounds_from_bb(element.get_BoundingBox(plan),plan) is None:return False\r\n        return True\r\n    except Exception:return False\r\n\r\n\r\ndef resolve_reference_markers(plan,refs,targets):\r\n    \"\"\"Resolve sources from this sheet and original markers from Plan Detail.\r\n\r\n    IMPORTANT: Revit element IDs belong to a document, not a naming convention.\r\n    A recreated assembly may keep exactly the same SheetNumber and view names\r\n    while having completely different IDs. Never hide an element from a stale ID.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    eligible=set(enum_num(t) for t in (ViewType.Detail,ViewType.Section,ViewType.DraftingView))\r\n    cats=_marker_categories()\r\n    # A view-scoped collector contains marker graphics visible/owned by Plan Detail.\r\n    all_in_plan=list(FilteredElementCollector(DOC,plan.Id).WhereElementIsNotElementType())\r\n    checked=[]\r\n    for item in refs:\r\n        name=str(item['name'])\r\n        axis=item['axis']\r\n        if axis not in ('vertical','horizontal'):\r\n            raise ValueError('axis must be vertical or horizontal: '+name)\r\n        if item['head_end'] not in ('positive','negative'):\r\n            raise ValueError('head_end invalid: '+name)\r\n        role=('left' if axis=='vertical' else 'front')\r\n        src=targets[role][1]\r\n        if str(src.Name).strip().lower()!=name.strip().lower():\r\n            raise ValueError('Placed source view name mismatch for %s: found %s'%(name,src.Name))\r\n        if enum_num(src.ViewType) not in eligible:\r\n            raise ValueError('%s source is not an eligible Detail/Section/Drafting view'%name)\r\n\r\n        candidates=[e for e in all_in_plan if _is_marker_candidate(e,plan,name,cats)\r\n                    and elem_num(e)!=elem_num(src)]\r\n        details=[_candidate_marker_info(e,plan) for e in candidates]\r\n        # First require an unhidden/hideable marker matching the view name.\r\n        visible=[(e,d) for e,d in zip(candidates,details)\r\n                 if d['hidden'] is False and d['can_hide'] and d['bbox_in_plan_ft'] is not None]\r\n        # Prefer a marker whose reference API confirms the same destination.\r\n        linked=[pair for pair in visible if pair[1]['linked_view_id']==elem_num(src)]\r\n        if len(linked)==1:\r\n            selected=linked[0]\r\n        elif len(linked)>1:\r\n            raise ValueError('%s has multiple markers linked to view %s: %s; no edits'%(\r\n                name,elem_num(src),[d['id'] for e,d in linked]))\r\n        elif len(visible)==1:\r\n            selected=visible[0]\r\n        else:\r\n            # No guessing. Report the actual document view ID and candidate IDs\r\n            # so a user can resolve the ambiguity without hiding arbitrary graphics.\r\n            raise ValueError('Cannot uniquely identify original %s marker in Plan Detail. '\r\n                             'source_view_id=%s; candidate_markers=%s; eligible_visible=%s. '\r\n                             'Run on clean initial sheet; do not rerun after replacement.'%(\r\n                name,elem_num(src),[d['id'] for d in details],\r\n                [d['id'] for e,d in visible]))\r\n        old,detail=selected\r\n        resolved=dict(item)\r\n        resolved['view_id']=elem_num(src)\r\n        resolved['marker_id']=elem_num(old)\r\n        checked.append({'name':name,'source':src,'original':old,'item':resolved,\r\n                        'resolution':{'source_from_placed_view_id':elem_num(src),\r\n                                      'original_marker_id':elem_num(old),\r\n                                      'marker_category':detail['category'],\r\n                                      'old_config_view_id':item.get('view_id'),\r\n                                      'old_config_marker_id':item.get('marker_id')}})\r\n    if len(set(elem_num(x['source']) for x in checked))!=len(checked):\r\n        raise ValueError('Source views for the two section references are the same')\r\n    if len(set(elem_num(x['original']) for x in checked))!=len(checked):\r\n        raise ValueError('Original markers for the two references are the same')\r\n    return checked\r\n\r\n\r\ndef validate_reference_sources(plan,refs,targets=None):\r\n    if targets is None:\r\n        raise ValueError('Dynamic source discovery requires placed sheet targets')\r\n    return resolve_reference_markers(plan,refs,targets)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef model_bounds(plan,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Bounds of visible model elements, projected into Plan Detail coordinates.\r\n\r\n    This is not a guaranteed assembly subset. The report gives the measured\r\n    bounds and element count; unusual models require a project-specific filter.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    boxes=[]; ids=[]\r\n    # Visible elements in the parent view only; section markers are non-model.\r\n    for element in FilteredElementCollector(DOC,plan.Id).WhereElementIsNotElementType():\r\n        try:\r\n            if element.Category is None or element.Category.CategoryType!=CategoryType.Model:\r\n                continue\r\n            bb=element.get_BoundingBox(plan)\r\n            r=bounds_from_bb(bb,plan)\r\n            if r is None or r.w<=0 or r.h<=0:continue\r\n            boxes.append(r)\r\n            ids.append(elem_num(element))\r\n        except Exception:continue\r\n    if len(boxes)<int(cfg['min_model_element_count']):\r\n        raise ValueError('Insufficient visible model elements in Plan Detail to locate assembly')\r\n    rect=Rect(min(r.x0 for r in boxes),min(r.y0 for r in boxes),\r\n              max(r.x1 for r in boxes),max(r.y1 for r in boxes))\r\n    # Fail closed when model geometry bounds are unreasonable.\r\n    crop=plan.CropBox\r\n    if crop is not None:\r\n        crop_w=abs(crop.Max.X-crop.Min.X);crop_h=abs(crop.Max.Y-crop.Min.Y)\r\n        if rect.w>max(5,crop_w*1.6) or rect.h>max(5,crop_h*1.6):\r\n            raise ValueError('Model bounds exceed 160% of Plan crop; likely non-assembly geometry. Refine model filter.')\r\n    return rect,ids\r\n\r\n\r\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n# v6.18.2: HIDDEN X section marker in Elevation Left, pointing DOWN at Plan Detail\r\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\ndef _x_marker_info(element,left,plan):\r\n    details={'id':elem_num(element),'name':str(element.Name),\r\n             'class':str(element.GetType().Name),\r\n             'is_hidden_in_elevation_left':None,'bbox_source':None,\r\n             'center_left_local_ft':None,'linked_view_id':None,\r\n             'bbox_left_rect_ft':None,'owner_view_id':None}\r\n    try:details['owner_view_id']=elem_num(element.OwnerViewId)\r\n    except Exception:pass\r\n    try:details['is_hidden_in_elevation_left']=bool(element.IsHidden(left))\r\n    except Exception:pass\r\n    try:details['category_hidden_in_elevation_left']=bool(left.GetCategoryHidden(element.Category.Id))\r\n    except Exception:details['category_hidden_in_elevation_left']=False\r\n    details['hidden_by_element_or_category']=(details['is_hidden_in_elevation_left'] is True or\r\n                                              details['category_hidden_in_elevation_left'] is True)\r\n    try:\r\n        ref_id=elem_num(ReferenceableViewUtils.GetReferencedViewId(DOC,element.Id))\r\n        details['linked_view_id']=ref_id if isinstance(ref_id,int) and ref_id>0 else None\r\n    except Exception:pass\r\n    for which,view in [('left_view',left),('world_bbox',None)]:\r\n        try:\r\n            bbox=element.get_BoundingBox(view)\r\n            if bbox is not None:\r\n                mid=XYZ((bbox.Min.X+bbox.Max.X)/2.0,\r\n                        (bbox.Min.Y+bbox.Max.Y)/2.0,\r\n                        (bbox.Min.Z+bbox.Max.Z)/2.0)\r\n                pt=bbox.Transform.OfPoint(mid)\r\n                q=pt.Subtract(left.Origin)\r\n                details['bbox_source']=which\r\n                details['center_left_local_ft']=[round(q.DotProduct(left.RightDirection),4),\r\n                                                  round(q.DotProduct(left.UpDirection),4),\r\n                                                  round(q.DotProduct(left.ViewDirection),4)]\r\n                try:\r\n                    coords=[]\r\n                    for bx in (bbox.Min.X,bbox.Max.X):\r\n                        for by in (bbox.Min.Y,bbox.Max.Y):\r\n                            for bz in (bbox.Min.Z,bbox.Max.Z):\r\n                                qp=bbox.Transform.OfPoint(XYZ(bx,by,bz)).Subtract(left.Origin)\r\n                                coords.append((qp.DotProduct(left.RightDirection),qp.DotProduct(left.UpDirection)))\r\n                    details['bbox_left_rect_ft']=[round(min(v[0] for v in coords),4),\r\n                                                 round(min(v[1] for v in coords),4),\r\n                                                 round(max(v[0] for v in coords),4),\r\n                                                 round(max(v[1] for v in coords),4)]\r\n                except Exception:pass\r\n                break\r\n        except Exception:pass\r\n    return details\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _assembly_spatial_bounds_for_x(plan,left,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Collect ALL assembly members' WORLD 3D bounds; no 2D view cropping.\r\n\r\n    That is crucial here: currently hidden/missing elements in Elevation Left\r\n    must still contribute to the top placement for the X section cutting line.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    aid=plan.AssociatedAssemblyInstanceId\r\n    assembly=DOC.GetElement(aid)\r\n    if assembly is None or not isinstance(assembly,AssemblyInstance):\r\n        raise ValueError('Plan Detail does not have an associated AssemblyInstance; cannot safely derive full top')\r\n    ids=[];up=[];right=[];depth=[];missing=[]\r\n    for mid in assembly.GetMemberIds():\r\n        el=DOC.GetElement(mid)\r\n        if el is None:continue\r\n        try:\r\n            cat=el.Category\r\n            if cat is None or cat.CategoryType!=CategoryType.Model:continue\r\n            bb=el.get_BoundingBox(None) # full model, not cropped by Elevation Left\r\n            if bb is None:\r\n                missing.append(elem_num(el));continue\r\n            b=bb.Transform\r\n            for x in (bb.Min.X,bb.Max.X):\r\n                for y in (bb.Min.Y,bb.Max.Y):\r\n                    for z in (bb.Min.Z,bb.Max.Z):\r\n                        pt=b.OfPoint(XYZ(x,y,z)).Subtract(left.Origin)\r\n                        up.append(pt.DotProduct(left.UpDirection))\r\n                        right.append(pt.DotProduct(left.RightDirection))\r\n                        depth.append(pt.DotProduct(left.ViewDirection))\r\n            ids.append(elem_num(el))\r\n        except Exception:\r\n            missing.append(elem_num(el))\r\n    if not up:\r\n        raise ValueError('Assembly has no usable world-space bounding boxes for full member geometry')\r\n    if missing:\r\n        raise ValueError('Cannot confirm full assembly top: %d member bounding boxes are missing (%s)'%(\r\n            len(missing),missing[:12]))\r\n    return {'assembly_id':elem_num(assembly),'member_ids':sorted(set(ids)),\r\n            'left_local_xmin':min(right),'left_local_xmax':max(right),\r\n            'left_local_ymin':min(up),'left_local_ymax':max(up),\r\n            'left_local_depth_min':min(depth),'left_local_depth_max':max(depth),\r\n            'assembly_height_ft':max(up)-min(up)}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _x_candidate_geometry_near(info,assembly,left,plan,check_horizontal=False):\r\n    \"\"\"Coarse locality check for unpaired candidates. Does NOT identify the source view.\"\"\"\r\n    pt=info.get('center_left_local_ft')\r\n    if pt is None:return False\r\n    w=assembly['left_local_xmax']-assembly['left_local_xmin']\r\n    h=assembly['left_local_ymax']-assembly['left_local_ymin']\r\n    rect=info.get('bbox_left_rect_ft')\r\n    # A section marker can have a very long line. Permit its bbox midpoint to\r\n    # lie farther away than the pipe center by half the actual line's length.\r\n    ex=0.5*abs(rect[2]-rect[0]) if rect else 0.0\r\n    ey=0.5*abs(rect[3]-rect[1]) if rect else 0.0\r\n    pad_x=max(mm_to_ft(1000),w*1.2,ex)\r\n    pad_y=max(mm_to_ft(700),h*1.2,ey)\r\n    if not (assembly['left_local_xmin']-pad_x<=pt[0]<=assembly['left_local_xmax']+pad_x):return False\r\n    if not (assembly['left_local_ymin']-pad_y<=pt[1]<=assembly['left_local_ymax']+pad_y):return False\r\n    if check_horizontal:\r\n        if rect is None:return False\r\n        width=rect[2]-rect[0];height=rect[3]-rect[1]\r\n        if width < max(mm_to_ft(40),height*1.5):return False\r\n    return True\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _x_marker_category_confirmed(element):\r\n    \"\"\"True for section-viewer originals; don't confuse a marker with the ViewSection.\"\"\"\r\n    if element is None or isinstance(element,ViewSection):return False\r\n    cat=getattr(element,'Category',None)\r\n    if cat is None:return False\r\n    try:\r\n        if elem_num(cat.Id) in _marker_categories():return True\r\n    except Exception:pass\r\n    try:\r\n        return str(cat.Name).strip().lower() in (\r\n            'views','sections','reference viewer','reference viewers','section line')\r\n    except Exception:return False\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _x_marker_match(e,left,plan,assembly,aliases,paired=False):\r\n    \"\"\"Validate origin-view identity without relying on UI selection.\r\n\r\n    The -1 pairing is a MODEL-DERIVED hint, not an unconditional guarantee:\r\n    source ViewSection Id and adjacent original viewer IDs were confirmed in\r\n    the user's prior Revit test; category, name/linked identity are checked.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    if not _x_marker_category_confirmed(e):return None,'not_section_viewer_category'\r\n    info=_x_marker_info(e,left,plan)\r\n    if info.get('linked_view_id') not in (None,elem_num(plan)):\r\n        return None,'linked_to_another_view'\r\n    nm=str(e.Name).strip().lower()\r\n    named=(nm==str(plan.Name).strip().lower() or nm in aliases)\r\n    linked=(info.get('linked_view_id')==elem_num(plan))\r\n    hidden=bool(info.get('hidden_by_element_or_category'))\r\n    near=_x_candidate_geometry_near(info,assembly,left,plan,False)\r\n    horizontal=_x_candidate_geometry_near(info,assembly,left,plan,True)\r\n    info['source_id_minus_one_pair']=bool(paired)\r\n    info['name_matches_plan_or_x']=bool(named)\r\n    info['linked_to_plan']=bool(linked)\r\n    info['geometry_near_assembly']=bool(near)\r\n    info['looks_horizontal_when_measurable']=bool(horizontal)\r\n    # In Revit, original section lines can be hidden by crop or view settings,\r\n    # not just Element.IsHidden or View.GetCategoryHidden. DO NOT require those\r\n    # flags for a strongly verified view/marker pair, but preserve both flags.\r\n    if paired:\r\n        # Some Revit original section marker elements have an internal/renamed\r\n        # Name unlike the source view's title. A hidden, geometrically aligned\r\n        # horizontal section at ViewSection.Id-1 is still a strong pairing.\r\n        generic_marker_name=(any(word in nm for word in ('section','detail','marker','viewer'))\r\n                             and not nm.startswith('elevation '))\r\n        if not (named or linked or (hidden and horizontal and generic_marker_name)):\r\n            return None,'paired_id_not_confirmed_by_name_link_or_generic_hidden_horizontal_marker'\r\n        return info,None\r\n    # Without the strong source-view pair, require linked or matching name,\r\n    # and that the element is hidden (or its bbox proves local horizontal cut).\r\n    if linked:\r\n        if hidden or near or info.get('center_left_local_ft') is None:return info,None\r\n        return None,'linked_but_far_from_elevation_left'\r\n    if named:\r\n        if hidden and (near or info.get('center_left_local_ft') is None):return info,None\r\n        if horizontal:return info,None\r\n        return None,'named_but_not_hidden_and_not_horizontal_near_assembly'\r\n    return None,'cannot_verify_plan_detail_identity'\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _document_x_marker_candidates(left,plan,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Discover original viewers document-wide, INCLUDING hidden annotations.\r\n\r\n    First try fast native category collectors. Fall back to a filtered full\r\n    document scan if Revit returns an empty/partial category inventory.\r\n    The view-scoped collector was unsuitable because it excludes RH elements.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    output=[];seen=set()\r\n    for name in ('OST_Viewers','OST_Sections','OST_ReferenceViewer'):\r\n        try:\r\n            for e in FilteredElementCollector(DOC).OfCategory(getattr(BuiltInCategory,name)).WhereElementIsNotElementType():\r\n                try:\r\n                    n=elem_num(e)\r\n                    if n in seen:continue\r\n                    if not _x_marker_category_confirmed(e):continue\r\n                    seen.add(n);output.append(e)\r\n                except Exception:continue\r\n        except Exception:continue\r\n    # Some Revit builds represent section-viewer graphics in a category not\r\n    # returned by the three native category filters. Broaden if none of those\r\n    # elements is even potentially associated with this Plan Detail view.\r\n    preferred=str(plan.Name).strip().lower()\r\n    aliases=[str(n).strip().lower() for n in cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_names',[])]\r\n    has_plausible=any((str(e.Name).strip().lower()==preferred or\r\n                       str(e.Name).strip().lower() in aliases)\r\n                      for e in output)\r\n    if not output or not has_plausible:\r\n        try:\r\n            for e in FilteredElementCollector(DOC).WhereElementIsNotElementType():\r\n                try:\r\n                    n=elem_num(e)\r\n                    if n not in seen and _x_marker_category_confirmed(e):\r\n                        seen.add(n);output.append(e)\r\n                except Exception:continue\r\n        except Exception:pass\r\n    return output\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _x_resolve_hidden_marker(left,plan,cfg,assembly):\r\n    \"\"\"Fully automatic source-linked discovery of original Plan Detail section.\r\n\r\n    1. Try the marker element immediately preceding Plan Detail ViewSection.Id.\r\n       This source-linked relation was seen in the user's original-marker tests\r\n       and has also been reported in Revit API community discussions.\r\n    2. Try a document-wide inventory: unique linked section/viewer or uniquely\r\n       named Plan Detail / X marker, validated against Elevation Left geometry.\r\n    3. Fail CLOSED if still ambiguous. NO selection or Element ID required.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    aliases=[str(n).strip().lower() for n in cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_names',[]) if str(n).strip()]\r\n    plan_id=elem_num(plan)\r\n    probe={'method':'automatic_source_view_relationship',\r\n           'plan_detail_view_id':plan_id,\r\n           'expected_original_marker_id':plan_id-1,\r\n           'ui_selection_used':False,'manual_marker_id_used':False}\r\n    paired=DOC.GetElement(eid(plan_id-1))\r\n    if paired is not None:\r\n        info,reason=_x_marker_match(paired,left,plan,assembly,aliases,paired=True)\r\n        probe['paired_marker_examined']=(info if info is not None else\r\n            {'id':elem_num(paired),'name':str(paired.Name),\r\n             'rejected_reason':reason})\r\n        if info is not None:\r\n            probe.update({'status':'automatic_source_view_id_pair',\r\n                          'selected_id':elem_num(paired),'selected':info,\r\n                          'candidate_count':1,\r\n                          'visibility_note':('explicitly_hidden' if info['hidden_by_element_or_category']\r\n                                             else 'hidden_other_way_or_currently_visible; visibility preserved')})\r\n            return paired,probe\r\n    else:probe['paired_marker_examined']={'status':'id_not_in_document'}\r\n    # Adjacent original marker elements may be linked to the same view while\r\n    # the marker ID is NOT exactly the view id - 1. Test a small range first.\r\n    local=[]\r\n    for offset in range(-12,13):\r\n        if offset in (-1,0):continue\r\n        n=plan_id+offset\r\n        if n<=0:continue\r\n        e=DOC.GetElement(eid(n))\r\n        if e is None:continue\r\n        info,reason=_x_marker_match(e,left,plan,assembly,aliases,paired=False)\r\n        if info is not None:\r\n            local.append((e,info))\r\n    local_unique={elem_num(e):(e,info) for e,info in local}\r\n    if len(local_unique)==1:\r\n        e,info=next(iter(local_unique.values()))\r\n        if info['linked_to_plan'] or (info['name_matches_plan_or_x'] and info['hidden_by_element_or_category']):\r\n            probe.update({'status':'automatic_near_source_view_id',\r\n                          'selected_id':elem_num(e),'selected':info,\r\n                          'near_source_candidates':len(local_unique)})\r\n            return e,probe\r\n    # Full document fallback: does not depend on UI selection or a known ID.\r\n    catalog=_document_x_marker_candidates(left,plan,cfg)\r\n    linked=[];named=[];unnamed_near=[];examined=[];rejected=[]\r\n    for element in catalog:\r\n        try:\r\n            info,reason=_x_marker_match(element,left,plan,assembly,aliases,paired=False)\r\n            if info is None:\r\n                if len(rejected)<8 and reason=='linked_to_another_view':\r\n                    rejected.append({'id':elem_num(element),'reason':reason})\r\n                continue\r\n            if info['linked_to_plan']:linked.append((element,info))\r\n            elif info['name_matches_plan_or_x']:named.append((element,info))\r\n            if len(examined)<35:examined.append(info)\r\n        except Exception:continue\r\n    # Prefer the specific plan link, then the exact Plan Detail name over X.\r\n    # Do NOT silently pick a geometrically nearest anonymous marker: another\r\n    # section can cross the same assembly, and moving it changes real cut planes.\r\n    def unique_by_id(pairs):return list({elem_num(e):(e,inf) for e,inf in pairs}.values())\r\n    linked=unique_by_id(linked)\r\n    if len(linked)==1:\r\n        element,info=linked[0]\r\n        probe.update({'status':'automatic_unique_linked_marker','selected_id':elem_num(element),\r\n                      'selected':info,'candidate_count':len(catalog)})\r\n        return element,probe\r\n    if len(linked)>1:\r\n        probe.update({'status':'ambiguous_linked_markers','candidates':[inf for e,inf in linked][:20]})\r\n        return None,probe\r\n    named=unique_by_id(named)\r\n    exact_name=[(e,i) for e,i in named if str(e.Name).strip().lower()==str(plan.Name).strip().lower()]\r\n    if len(exact_name)==1:\r\n        element,info=exact_name[0]\r\n        probe.update({'status':'automatic_unique_plan_name','selected_id':elem_num(element),\r\n                      'selected':info,'candidate_count':len(catalog)})\r\n        return element,probe\r\n    if len(exact_name)==0 and len(named)==1:\r\n        element,info=named[0]\r\n        probe.update({'status':'automatic_unique_x_alias','selected_id':elem_num(element),\r\n                      'selected':info,'candidate_count':len(catalog)})\r\n        return element,probe\r\n    probe.update({'status':'ambiguous' if named or len(local_unique)>1 else 'missing',\r\n                  'all_viewer_elements_examined':len(catalog),\r\n                  'near_source_view_candidates':[i for e,i in local][:15],\r\n                  'named_candidates':[i for e,i in named][:20],\r\n                  'other_inspected_candidates':examined[:25],\r\n                  'excluded_cross_view_candidates':rejected,\r\n                  'reason':'No uniquely verified original Plan Detail section marker. '\r\n                           'No marker was moved; see candidate diagnostics.'})\r\n    return None,probe\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _x_marker_center_y(marker,left):\r\n    info=_x_marker_info(marker,left,None)\r\n    center=info['center_left_local_ft']\r\n    return (float(center[1]),info) if center is not None else (None,info)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef adjust_elevation_left_hidden_x_to_top(targets,cfg,scale,baseline_plan_ids=None):\r\n    \"\"\"Move hidden original 'X' Plan Detail section cut UP in Elevation Left.\r\n\r\n    Runs inside EXISTING layout trial/apply Revit transaction; changes the REAL\r\n    Plan Detail cut plane, not just the graphic. Original hidden state retained.\r\n    Returns diagnostic and fails if prior visible plan model elements disappear.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    if not cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_to_top',True):\r\n        return {'status':'disabled','moved':False}\r\n    left=targets['left'][1]; plan=targets['plan'][1]\r\n    if not isinstance(plan,ViewSection):\r\n        return {'status':'unsupported_plan_not_section_view','moved':False}\r\n    # Source ViewDirection is a camera vector, not the drawn section head. In\r\n    # the user's actual Revit file its dot with Left.UpDirection was +1 while\r\n    # bubble 2 visibly pointed DOWN. Preserve graphic direction; move only Y.\r\n    facing=plan.ViewDirection.Normalize().DotProduct(left.UpDirection.Normalize())\r\n    if cfg.get('_x_marker_preflight_missing') is not None:\r\n        if cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_missing_policy','error')=='error':\r\n            raise ValueError('X marker discovery failed: '+str(cfg['_x_marker_preflight_missing'])[:850])\r\n        return {'status':'skipped_marker_not_found','moved':False,\r\n                'discovery':cfg['_x_marker_preflight_missing']}\r\n    assembly=cfg.get('_x_assembly_spatial') or _assembly_spatial_bounds_for_x(plan,left,cfg)\r\n    marker,discovery=_x_resolve_hidden_marker(left,plan,cfg,assembly)\r\n    if marker is None:\r\n        if cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_missing_policy','skip')=='error':\r\n            raise ValueError('Cannot identify hidden X section marker: '+str(discovery)[:800])\r\n        return {'status':'skipped_marker_not_found','moved':False,\r\n                'discovery':discovery,'assembly_id':assembly['assembly_id']}\r\n    if marker.Pinned:\r\n        raise ValueError('Hidden X section marker is pinned; refusing to move it')\r\n    before_hidden=bool(marker.IsHidden(left))\r\n    before_category_hidden=bool(left.GetCategoryHidden(marker.Category.Id))\r\n    # The original marker can also be suppressed by view crop or annotation\r\n    # settings, which do not always set Element.IsHidden. We have already\r\n    # verified its source-view identity; keep the exact visibility state.\r\n    if baseline_plan_ids is None:\r\n        _,baseline_plan_ids=model_bounds(plan,cfg)\r\n    before_plan_ids=set(baseline_plan_ids)\r\n    before_annotations=set(_visible_source_annotation_ids(plan))\r\n    gap_mm=float(cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_gap_mm',30.0))\r\n    if not 2.0<=gap_mm<=50.0:raise ValueError('elevation_left_hidden_x_gap_mm must be 2..50')\r\n    target=assembly['left_local_ymax']+mm_to_ft(gap_mm*scale)\r\n    center_y,marker_before=_x_marker_center_y(marker,left)\r\n    # Source view Origin can shift independently of the displayed marker after\r\n    # direct mirroring (confirmed by the user's Revit probe). NEVER use that\r\n    # Origin as a substitute when the hidden original marker has no bbox.\r\n    locator='actual_original_marker_bbox_center'\r\n    if center_y is None:\r\n        if not cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_allow_plan_origin_fallback',True):\r\n            return {'status':'skipped_unmeasurable_original_marker','moved':False,\r\n                    'marker_id':elem_num(marker),'discovery':discovery}\r\n        # Unlike Elevation Front, the Plan Detail original is NOT mirrored in\r\n        # this workflow. Its source origin can be used as a cautious fallback,\r\n        # but ONLY if it lies within the actual assembly's vertical vicinity\r\n        # and it is independently validated after the marker transform.\r\n        center_y=plan.Origin.Subtract(left.Origin).DotProduct(left.UpDirection)\r\n        pad=max(mm_to_ft(500.0),assembly['assembly_height_ft']*0.5)\r\n        if not (assembly['left_local_ymin']-pad<=center_y<=assembly['left_local_ymax']+pad):\r\n            raise ValueError('Unmeasurable X graphic; Plan Detail Origin is outside assembly neighborhood')\r\n        locator='plan_detail_cut_origin_fallback_verified_after_move'\r\n    delta=target-center_y\r\n    move_mm=delta*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n    max_move=float(cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_max_move_mm',180.0))\r\n    if abs(move_mm)>max_move:\r\n        raise ValueError('Hidden X cut needs %.2f paper-mm move, over cap %.2fmm'%(move_mm,max_move))\r\n    if abs(move_mm)>float(cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_tolerance_mm',0.8)):\r\n        ElementTransformUtils.MoveElement(DOC,marker.Id,left.UpDirection.Normalize().Multiply(delta))\r\n        DOC.Regenerate()\r\n    after_marker=DOC.GetElement(marker.Id)\r\n    after_plan=DOC.GetElement(plan.Id)\r\n    if after_marker is None or after_plan is None:\r\n        raise ValueError('X marker/source view missing after moving')\r\n    if bool(after_marker.IsHidden(left))!=before_hidden or bool(left.GetCategoryHidden(after_marker.Category.Id))!=before_category_hidden:\r\n        raise ValueError('Original X marker visibility or category hidden state changed')\r\n    final_y,after_info=_x_marker_center_y(after_marker,left)\r\n    if locator=='plan_detail_cut_origin_fallback_verified_after_move':\r\n        # Model may have no visible bounds for hidden graphics, so verify by\r\n        # the same unchanged source-view anchor before and after movement.\r\n        final_y=after_plan.Origin.Subtract(left.Origin).DotProduct(left.UpDirection)\r\n    if final_y is None:\r\n        raise ValueError('Lost hidden X marker positioning evidence after movement; rollback')\r\n    error_mm=(final_y-target)*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n    if abs(error_mm)>float(cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_tolerance_mm',0.8)):\r\n        raise ValueError('Original hidden X cut did not reach target top: %.2f paper-mm error'%error_mm)\r\n    _,after_ids=model_bounds(after_plan,cfg)\r\n    lost=sorted(before_plan_ids-set(after_ids))\r\n    if lost:\r\n        raise ValueError('Moving X cut removed %d previously visible Plan Detail model elements: %s'%(\r\n             len(lost),lost[:15]))\r\n    missing_annotations=sorted(before_annotations-set(_visible_source_annotation_ids(after_plan)))\r\n    if missing_annotations:\r\n        raise ValueError('Moving X cut removed Plan Detail annotations: %s'%missing_annotations[:15])\r\n    assembly_ids=set(assembly['member_ids'])\r\n    before_members=sorted(before_plan_ids & assembly_ids)\r\n    after_members=sorted(set(after_ids) & assembly_ids)\r\n    missing_members=sorted(assembly_ids-set(after_ids))\r\n    if missing_members and cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_require_all_members_visible',False):\r\n        raise ValueError('Plan Detail still misses %d model assembly members: %s' %(\r\n           len(missing_members),missing_members[:20]))\r\n    return {'status':'adjusted_to_top' if abs(move_mm)>float(cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_tolerance_mm',0.8))\r\n            else 'already_at_top',\r\n            'moved':abs(move_mm)>float(cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_tolerance_mm',0.8)),\r\n            'marker_id':elem_num(marker),'source_plan_view_id':elem_num(after_plan),\r\n            'elevation_left_view_id':elem_num(left),'original_visibility_state_preserved':True,\r\n            'hidden_by_element':before_hidden,'hidden_by_category':before_category_hidden,\r\n            'assembly_id':assembly['assembly_id'],\r\n            'marker_before':marker_before,'marker_after':after_info,\r\n            'discovery':discovery,'locator':locator,\r\n            'head_direction_preserved_not_edited':True,\r\n            'head_direction_api_verified':False,\r\n            'facing_dot_diagnostic_only':round(facing,4),\r\n            'full_assembly_model_height_ft':round(assembly['assembly_height_ft'],4),\r\n            'target_height_above_assembly_paper_mm':gap_mm,\r\n            'requested_shift_up_paper_mm':round(move_mm,3),\r\n            'final_height_error_paper_mm':round(error_mm,3),\r\n            'plan_visible_model_count_before':len(before_plan_ids),\r\n            'plan_visible_model_count_after':len(after_ids),\r\n            'assembly_members_visible_before':len(before_members),\r\n            'assembly_members_visible_after':len(after_members),\r\n            'assembly_members_still_not_visible':missing_members[:30],\r\n            'requires_visual_QA':True}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef try_elevation_left_x_with_subtransaction(targets,cfg,scale,baseline_plan_ids=None):\r\n    \"\"\"Keep the working v6.17 layout intact when Revit rejects the new X move.\r\n\r\n    X is an optional experimental edit. Roll back ONLY that edit on unexpected\r\n    failure, report it, and let the existing marker/layout solver proceed.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    if not cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_to_top',True):\r\n        return {'status':'disabled','moved':False}\r\n    child=SubTransaction(DOC)\r\n    child.Start()\r\n    try:\r\n        diagnostic=adjust_elevation_left_hidden_x_to_top(\r\n            targets,cfg,scale,baseline_plan_ids=baseline_plan_ids)\r\n        if diagnostic.get('status','').startswith('skipped'):\r\n            state=child.RollBack()\r\n            if state!=TransactionStatus.RolledBack:\r\n                raise ValueError('X marker subtransaction failed to roll back')\r\n            diagnostic['subtransaction_rolled_back']=True\r\n            if cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_missing_policy','error')=='error':\r\n                raise ValueError('Hidden X marker was not adjusted: '+str(diagnostic)[:650])\r\n        else:\r\n            state=child.Commit()\r\n            if state!=TransactionStatus.Committed:\r\n                raise ValueError('X marker subtransaction failed to commit into parent trial')\r\n            diagnostic['subtransaction_committed_into_parent_trial']=True\r\n        DOC.Regenerate()\r\n        return diagnostic\r\n    except Exception as exc:\r\n        try:\r\n            if child.GetStatus()==TransactionStatus.Started:\r\n                state=child.RollBack()\r\n                if state!=TransactionStatus.RolledBack:\r\n                    raise ValueError('X marker subtransaction rollback status not RolledBack')\r\n            else:\r\n                if child.GetStatus()!=TransactionStatus.RolledBack:\r\n                    raise ValueError('X marker subtransaction state uncertain: '+str(child.GetStatus()))\r\n        except Exception as rollback_exc:\r\n            # Cannot safely continue the main sheet transaction.\r\n            raise ValueError('X marker subtransaction rollback FAILED: '+str(rollback_exc))\r\n        if cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_missing_policy','skip')=='error':\r\n            raise ValueError('Elevation Left hidden X failed: '+str(exc)[:350])\r\n        DOC.Regenerate()\r\n        return {'status':'skipped_x_error_rolled_back','moved':False,\r\n                'error':str(exc)[:650],'subtransaction_rolled_back':True}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef reference_plane_anchor(plan, src, old, settings, cfg, scale):\r\n    \"\"\"Project source view cut plane to Plan Detail and validate original symbol location.\r\n\r\n    The public API does not expose manually edited head/tail grips. This uses\r\n    an actual source cut plane and refuses changes that deviate from it.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    n=plan.ViewDirection.Normalize()\r\n    sn=src.ViewDirection.Normalize()\r\n    if abs(n.DotProduct(sn))>0.2:\r\n        raise ValueError('Source view %s is not perpendicular to Plan Detail' % src.Name)\r\n    original=src.Origin\r\n    q=original.Subtract(n.Multiply(original.Subtract(plan.Origin).DotProduct(n)))\r\n    in_plane_normal=sn.Subtract(n.Multiply(sn.DotProduct(n)))\r\n    denominator=in_plane_normal.DotProduct(in_plane_normal)\r\n    if denominator<1e-6:\r\n        raise ValueError('Source/Plan normals nearly parallel: '+src.Name)\r\n    q=q.Subtract(in_plane_normal.Multiply(q.Subtract(original).DotProduct(sn)/denominator))\r\n    axis=(plan.UpDirection if settings['axis']=='vertical'\r\n          else plan.RightDirection).Normalize()\r\n    alignment=abs(sn.CrossProduct(n).Normalize().DotProduct(axis))\r\n    if alignment<0.995:\r\n        raise ValueError('%s cut line not axis-aligned enough for shared-tail L: %.4f' %\r\n                         (src.Name,alignment))\r\n    mb=bounds_from_bb(old.get_BoundingBox(plan),plan)\r\n    if mb is None:\r\n        raise ValueError('Original marker box unavailable for '+src.Name)\r\n    lateral=q.Subtract(plan.Origin).DotProduct(\r\n        plan.RightDirection if settings['axis']=='vertical' else plan.UpDirection)\r\n    lo,hi=((mb.x0,mb.x1) if settings['axis']=='vertical' else (mb.y0,mb.y1))\r\n    tol=mm_to_ft(float(cfg['cut_line_tolerance_paper_mm'])*scale)\r\n    if lateral<lo-tol or lateral>hi+tol:\r\n        raise ValueError('%s cut plane differs from original marker; no replacement' % src.Name)\r\n    return q,sn,alignment,mb\r\n\r\n\r\ndef prepare_shared_tail_markers(plan,records,geometry,cfg,scale):\r\n    \"\"\"Create FULL geometry-spanning cut lines with visible trailing tail stubs.\r\n\r\n    v6.13: In geometry_proximity mode, draw the reference L just below/left\r\n    of actual visible assembly model geometry. The source cut planes are\r\n    verified but intentionally not used as the reference graphic location.\r\n    Source views and their crop are unchanged. Marker heads, reference links,\r\n    full measured model coverage, and visible 5 mm trailing stubs are retained.\r\n\r\n    In source_cut_plane mode the original v6.12 behavior is used verbatim.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    by_axis={r['item']['axis']:r for r in records}\r\n    if len(records)!=2 or set(by_axis)!=set(['vertical','horizontal']):\r\n        raise ValueError('Expected exactly one vertical and one horizontal reference')\r\n    if by_axis['vertical']['item']['head_end']!='positive':\r\n        raise ValueError('Vertical head must face upward')\r\n    if by_axis['horizontal']['item']['head_end']!='negative':\r\n        raise ValueError('Horizontal reference must be created head-left before mirroring')\r\n    plane={}\r\n    for axis,r in by_axis.items():\r\n        plane[axis]=reference_plane_anchor(plan,r['source'],r['original'],r['item'],cfg,scale)\r\n    vq=plane['vertical'][0];hq=plane['horizontal'][0]\r\n    origin=plan.Origin;right=plan.RightDirection.Normalize();up=plan.UpDirection.Normalize()\r\n    source_x=vq.Subtract(origin).DotProduct(right)\r\n    source_y=hq.Subtract(origin).DotProduct(up)\r\n    source_shared=origin.Add(right.Multiply(source_x)).Add(up.Multiply(source_y))\r\n    residuals={}\r\n    # Verify BOTH original source cut planes BEFORE any independent drawing\r\n    # adjustment. The user's existing elevations must remain intact.\r\n    for axis,r in by_axis.items():\r\n        residual=abs(source_shared.Subtract(r['source'].Origin).DotProduct(\r\n            r['source'].ViewDirection.Normalize()))*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n        residuals[axis]=round(residual,4)\r\n        if residual>float(cfg['shared_tail_cut_plane_tolerance_mm']):\r\n            raise ValueError('%s source cut plane misses original shared junction by %.3f paper mm' %\r\n                             (r['name'],residual))\r\n    paper_to_model=mm_to_ft(scale)\r\n    mode=str(cfg.get('marker_placement_mode','source_cut_plane'))\r\n    if mode not in ('source_cut_plane','geometry_proximity'):\r\n        raise ValueError('marker_placement_mode must be geometry_proximity or source_cut_plane')\r\n    shared_x=source_x\r\n    shared_y=source_y\r\n    if mode=='geometry_proximity':\r\n        # Both marker lines remain axis-aligned, forming a common L near the\r\n        # visible assembly. The assembly itself and the source Detail views\r\n        # are NEVER translated. Reference sections do not own source view crop.\r\n        gap_x=float(cfg.get('vertical_marker_clearance_from_geometry_mm',8.0))\r\n        gap_y=float(cfg.get('horizontal_marker_clearance_from_geometry_mm',8.0))\r\n        if not (2.0<=gap_x<=30.0 and 2.0<=gap_y<=30.0):\r\n            raise ValueError('Geometry-to-reference clearances must be 2..30 paper mm')\r\n        shared_x=geometry.x0-paper_to_model*gap_x\r\n        shared_y=geometry.y0-paper_to_model*gap_y\r\n        max_move=float(cfg.get('max_marker_move_from_source_mm',165.0))\r\n        dx_paper=abs(shared_x-source_x)*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n        dy_paper=abs(shared_y-source_y)*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n        if max(dx_paper,dy_paper)>max_move:\r\n            raise ValueError('Reference markers would move %.1f mm X / %.1f mm Y from source cut planes; '\r\n                             'limit %.1f mm. Adjust max_marker_move_from_source_mm only after reviewing '\r\n                             'reference semantics.'%(dx_paper,dy_paper,max_move))\r\n        if cfg.get('require_schematic_marker_confirmation',False) and not cfg.get('approve_schematic_markers',False):\r\n            raise ValueError('Geometry-proximity markers require explicit approve_schematic_markers=True')\r\n    shared=origin.Add(right.Multiply(shared_x)).Add(up.Multiply(shared_y))\r\n    offset_x=(shared_x-source_x)*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n    offset_y=(shared_y-source_y)*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n    geometry_height_mm=geometry.h*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n    geometry_width_mm=geometry.w*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n    ratio=float(cfg['vertical_marker_height_ratio'])\r\n    if not (.75<=ratio<=1.50):\r\n        raise ValueError('vertical_marker_height_ratio must be 0.75..1.50')\r\n    v_margin=float(cfg['vertical_geometry_margin_mm'])\r\n    h_margin=float(cfg['horizontal_geometry_margin_mm'])\r\n    v_stub=float(cfg['vertical_tail_stub_mm'])\r\n    h_stub=float(cfg['horizontal_tail_stub_mm'])\r\n    if min(v_margin,h_margin,v_stub,h_stub)<0:\r\n        raise ValueError('Marker margins and stubs cannot be negative')\r\n    if max(v_margin,h_margin,v_stub,h_stub)>30:\r\n        raise ValueError('Marker margin or trailing stub exceeds 30 mm')\r\n    v_tail_y=min(shared_y-paper_to_model*v_stub,\r\n                 geometry.y0-paper_to_model*v_margin)\r\n    v_target_length=max(float(cfg['vertical_min_length_paper_mm']),\r\n                        geometry_height_mm*ratio + 2*float(cfg['vertical_top_and_bottom_margin_mm']))\r\n    v_head_y=max(geometry.y1+paper_to_model*v_margin,\r\n                 v_tail_y+paper_to_model*v_target_length)\r\n    v_head=origin.Add(right.Multiply(shared_x)).Add(up.Multiply(v_head_y))\r\n    v_tail=origin.Add(right.Multiply(shared_x)).Add(up.Multiply(v_tail_y))\r\n    if cfg.get('horizontal_cover_all_plan_geometry',True):\r\n        h_tail_x=min(shared_x-paper_to_model*h_stub,\r\n                     geometry.x0-paper_to_model*h_margin)\r\n        h_head_x=max(shared_x+paper_to_model*float(cfg['horizontal_length_paper_mm']),\r\n                     geometry.x1+paper_to_model*h_margin)\r\n    else:\r\n        h_tail_x=shared_x-paper_to_model*h_stub\r\n        h_head_x=shared_x+paper_to_model*float(cfg['horizontal_length_paper_mm'])\r\n    h_tail=origin.Add(right.Multiply(h_tail_x)).Add(up.Multiply(shared_y))\r\n    # Mirror about tail. The *created* head is to its left; reflection places\r\n    # the *final* head at h_head_x, to the right, preserving the upward symbol.\r\n    h_final_head=origin.Add(right.Multiply(h_head_x)).Add(up.Multiply(shared_y))\r\n    h_created_head=h_tail.Subtract(right.Multiply(h_head_x-h_tail_x))\r\n    vertical_mm=(v_head_y-v_tail_y)*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n    horizontal_mm=(h_head_x-h_tail_x)*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n    cap=float(cfg['marker_max_length_paper_mm'])\r\n    if vertical_mm>cap or horizontal_mm>cap:\r\n        raise ValueError('Required complete marker span exceeds %.0fmm: vertical %.1fmm, '\r\n                         'horizontal %.1fmm at 1:%d. Cannot trim visible geometry.' %\r\n                         (cap,vertical_mm,horizontal_mm,scale))\r\n    if vertical_mm<=0 or horizontal_mm<=0:\r\n        raise ValueError('Calculated marker length not positive')\r\n    heads={'vertical':v_head,'horizontal':h_created_head}\r\n    tails={'vertical':v_tail,'horizontal':h_tail}\r\n    output=[]\r\n    for axis in ('vertical','horizontal'):\r\n        r=by_axis[axis];head=heads[axis];tail=tails[axis];sn=plane[axis][1]\r\n        inferred=plan.ViewDirection.CrossProduct(head.Subtract(tail).Normalize()).Normalize()\r\n        facing_dot=inferred.DotProduct(sn)\r\n        out={\r\n          'name':r['name'],'source_view_id':elem_num(r['source']),\r\n          'original_marker_id':elem_num(r['original']),\r\n          'axis':axis,'shared_junction_xyz_ft':xyz_info(shared),\r\n          'original_source_cut_plane_junction_xyz_ft':xyz_info(source_shared),\r\n          'reference_marker_placement_mode':mode,\r\n          'reference_marker_is_schematic':mode=='geometry_proximity',\r\n          'marker_displacement_from_source_junction_mm':[round(offset_x,2),round(offset_y,2)],\r\n          'measured_geometry_to_vertical_line_mm':round((geometry.x0-shared_x)*FT_TO_MM/scale,2),\r\n          'measured_geometry_to_horizontal_line_mm':round((geometry.y0-shared_y)*FT_TO_MM/scale,2),\r\n          'creation_head_xyz_ft':xyz_info(head),\r\n          'expected_final_head_xyz_ft':xyz_info(h_final_head if axis=='horizontal' else head),\r\n          'tail_xyz_ft':xyz_info(tail),\r\n          'tail_at_shared_junction':False,\r\n          'tail_extension_from_junction_mm':round((shared_y-v_tail_y if axis=='vertical' else\r\n                                                  shared_x-h_tail_x)*FT_TO_MM/scale,2),\r\n          'minimum_tail_stub_requested_mm':round(v_stub if axis=='vertical' else h_stub,2),\r\n          'marker_length_paper_mm':round(vertical_mm if axis=='vertical' else horizontal_mm,2),\r\n          'assembly_model_width_paper_mm':round(geometry_width_mm,2),\r\n          'assembly_model_height_paper_mm':round(geometry_height_mm,2),\r\n          'full_model_geometry_covered':True if axis=='vertical' else\r\n                           bool(cfg.get('horizontal_cover_all_plan_geometry',True)),\r\n          'horizontal_geometry_margins_mm':(\r\n              [round((geometry.x0-h_tail_x)*FT_TO_MM/scale,2),\r\n               round((h_head_x-geometry.x1)*FT_TO_MM/scale,2)] if axis=='horizontal' else None),\r\n          'vertical_geometry_margins_mm':(\r\n              [round((geometry.y0-v_tail_y)*FT_TO_MM/scale,2),\r\n               round((v_head_y-geometry.y1)*FT_TO_MM/scale,2)] if axis=='vertical' else None),\r\n          'vertical_height_ratio':ratio,\r\n          'create_then_mirror':axis=='horizontal',\r\n          'mirror_plane_through_tail':axis=='horizontal',\r\n          'source_cut_plane_preserved':mode=='source_cut_plane',\r\n          'original_source_cut_planes_verified':True,\r\n          'shared_tail_plane_residual_mm':residuals[axis],\r\n          'axis_alignment':round(plane[axis][2],4),\r\n          'inferred_facing_dot':round(facing_dot,3),\r\n          'facing_reversed_vs_source':facing_dot < -.98,\r\n          'requires_visual_orientation_review':True,\r\n          'trailing_tail_policy':'crossing_stubs_at_reference_junction'\r\n        }\r\n        output.append((r,head,tail,out))\r\n    return output\r\n\r\n\r\ndef perform_replacement(parent,records,geometry,cfg,scale):\r\n    \"\"\"Create both references and mirror ONLY Elevation Front around its tail.\r\n\r\n    Identical path is used during rolled-back candidate trials AND final apply,\r\n    preventing a preview/apply geometry mismatch. Original reference markers\r\n    remain untouched until both replacements and link checks have succeeded.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    planned=prepare_shared_tail_markers(parent,records,geometry,cfg,scale)\r\n    created_ids=[]\r\n    diagnostics=[]\r\n    known_ids=set(elem_num(x) for x in parent.GetReferenceSections())\r\n    for record,head,tail,base_diag in planned:\r\n        diag=dict(base_diag)\r\n        # The original source DETAIL view is referenced; it is never recreated.\r\n        ViewSection.CreateReferenceSection(DOC,parent.Id,record['source'].Id,head,tail)\r\n        DOC.Regenerate()\r\n        ids_now=set(elem_num(x) for x in parent.GetReferenceSections())\r\n        new_ids=sorted(ids_now-known_ids)\r\n        if len(new_ids)!=1:\r\n            raise ValueError('%s: expected exactly one newly created reference; found %d' % (\r\n                record['name'],len(new_ids)))\r\n        new_id=eid(new_ids[0])\r\n        new_marker=DOC.GetElement(new_id)\r\n        if new_marker is None:\r\n            raise ValueError('%s reference is missing after creation' % record['name'])\r\n        diag['new_reference_element_id']=new_ids[0]\r\n        diag['mirror_attempted']=False\r\n        diag['mirror_succeeded']=False\r\n        if record['item']['axis']=='horizontal':\r\n            if not cfg.get('mirror_front_reference_about_tail',True):\r\n                raise ValueError('Create-then-mirror is required for the horizontal Elevation Front marker')\r\n            diag['mirror_attempted']=True\r\n            diag['can_mirror']=bool(ElementTransformUtils.CanMirrorElement(DOC,new_id))\r\n            if not diag['can_mirror']:\r\n                raise ValueError('Elevation Front marker cannot be mirrored in this Revit project. '\r\n                                 'Transaction will be rolled back.')\r\n            # This EXACT plane and API call worked in the user's isolated probe.\r\n            # Mirror normal is Plan Detail RIGHT, plane origin is fixed tail.\r\n            mirror_plane=Plane.CreateByNormalAndOrigin(parent.RightDirection.Normalize(),tail)\r\n            one_id=List[ElementId]()\r\n            one_id.Add(new_id)\r\n            ElementTransformUtils.MirrorElements(DOC,one_id,mirror_plane,False)\r\n            DOC.Regenerate()\r\n            new_marker=DOC.GetElement(new_id)\r\n            if new_marker is None:\r\n                raise ValueError('Elevation Front reference vanished after mirroring')\r\n            diag['mirror_succeeded']=True\r\n            diag['mirror_plane_origin_xyz_ft']=xyz_info(tail)\r\n            diag['mirror_plane_normal_xyz']=xyz_info(parent.RightDirection.Normalize())\r\n        # Verify that BOTH created reference symbols still refer to their\r\n        # original Detail views, especially after the Elevation Front mirror.\r\n        referenced_id=ReferenceableViewUtils.GetReferencedViewId(DOC,new_id)\r\n        diag['referenced_view_id_after']=elem_num(referenced_id)\r\n        diag['referenced_view_verified']=(elem_num(referenced_id)==elem_num(record['source']))\r\n        if not diag['referenced_view_verified']:\r\n            raise ValueError('%s marker no longer references the correct Detail view' % record['name'])\r\n        if new_marker.IsHidden(parent):\r\n            raise ValueError('New %s marker unexpectedly hidden in Plan Detail' % record['name'])\r\n        diag['mirrored_reference_model_bounds']=None\r\n        if diag['mirror_succeeded']:\r\n            bounds=bounds_from_bb(new_marker.get_BoundingBox(parent),parent)\r\n            diag['mirrored_reference_model_bounds']=None if bounds is None else [\r\n                round(bounds.x0,4),round(bounds.y0,4),round(bounds.x1,4),round(bounds.y1,4)]\r\n        diagnostics.append(diag)\r\n        created_ids.append(new_ids[0])\r\n        known_ids=ids_now\r\n\r\n    if len(created_ids)!=len(planned):\r\n        raise ValueError('Not all reference symbols were created')\r\n    originals=List[ElementId]()\r\n    for r in records:originals.Add(r['original'].Id)\r\n    parent.HideElements(originals)   # ONLY inside Plan Detail\r\n    DOC.Regenerate()\r\n    for r in records:\r\n        if not r['original'].IsHidden(parent):\r\n            raise ValueError('Original reference not hidden in Plan Detail: '+r['name'])\r\n    return diagnostics\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n# ---- v6.14 original section-marker operations (no replacement / no hiding) ----\r\ndef original_source_view_state(view):\r\n    \"\"\"Snapshot of attributes known to change after direct original mirroring.\"\"\"\r\n    def optional_vec(obj,attr):\r\n        try:return xyz_info(getattr(obj,attr))\r\n        except Exception:return None\r\n    state={'id':elem_num(view),'origin':optional_vec(view,'Origin'),\r\n           'direction':optional_vec(view,'ViewDirection'),\r\n           'up':optional_vec(view,'UpDirection'),\r\n           'right':optional_vec(view,'RightDirection'),\r\n           'scale':int(view.Scale)}\r\n    try:\r\n        crop=view.CropBox\r\n        state['crop_min']=xyz_info(crop.Min)\r\n        state['crop_max']=xyz_info(crop.Max)\r\n        state['crop_transform_origin']=xyz_info(crop.Transform.Origin)\r\n    except Exception as exc:\r\n        state['crop_error']=str(exc)[:100]\r\n    return state\r\n\r\n\r\ndef original_marker_mirror_pivot(marker,plan):\r\n    \"\"\"Exactly the bbox-center pivot from the SUCCESSFUL isolated probe.\"\"\"\r\n    bb=marker.get_BoundingBox(plan)\r\n    if bb is None:raise ValueError('Original marker bbox missing in Plan Detail: %s'%elem_num(marker))\r\n    center_local=XYZ((bb.Min.X+bb.Max.X)*.5,(bb.Min.Y+bb.Max.Y)*.5,\r\n                     (bb.Min.Z+bb.Max.Z)*.5)\r\n    center_world=bb.Transform.OfPoint(center_local)\r\n    normal=plan.ViewDirection.Normalize()\r\n    return center_world.Subtract(normal.Multiply(center_world.Subtract(plan.Origin).DotProduct(normal)))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _marker_plan_bounds(plan,records,geometry,scale):\r\n    \"\"\"Model + the actual two ORIGINAL marker boxes; no title/crop padding.\"\"\"\r\n    rects=[('model',geometry)]\r\n    for rec in records:\r\n        r=bounds_from_bb(rec['original'].get_BoundingBox(plan),plan)\r\n        if r is None:raise ValueError('Missing original marker geometry for '+rec['name'])\r\n        rects.append((rec['name'],r))\r\n    combined=Rect(min(r.x0 for _,r in rects),min(r.y0 for _,r in rects),\r\n                  max(r.x1 for _,r in rects),max(r.y1 for _,r in rects))\r\n    unit=FT_TO_MM/float(scale)\r\n    return {'extent_mm':[round(combined.w*unit,2),round(combined.h*unit,2)],\r\n            'area_mm2':round(combined.w*combined.h*unit*unit,2),\r\n            'parts_model_mm':{k:[round(v*unit,2) for v in (r.x0,r.y0,r.x1,r.y1)]\r\n                              for k,r in rects}}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _visible_source_annotation_ids(view):\r\n    \"\"\"Track visible annotation identity to detect unintended source tag loss.\"\"\"\r\n    ids=[]\r\n    for element in FilteredElementCollector(DOC,view.Id).WhereElementIsNotElementType():\r\n        try:\r\n            if (element.Category is not None and\r\n                    element.Category.CategoryType==CategoryType.Annotation and\r\n                    not element.IsHidden(view) and\r\n                    element.get_BoundingBox(view) is not None):\r\n                ids.append(elem_num(element))\r\n        except Exception:continue\r\n    return sorted(set(ids))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _crop_x_content_extents(view,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Visible source model + visible annotation bounds along CropBox local X.\r\n\r\n    Uses the original world-space bbox corners, transformed through CropBox\r\n    inverse. No assumed sign/orientation between view and crop transforms.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    cb=view.CropBox\r\n    if cb is None:raise ValueError('%s has no CropBox'%view.Name)\r\n    inverse=cb.Transform.Inverse\r\n    values=[]; ids=[]\r\n    for el in FilteredElementCollector(DOC,view.Id).WhereElementIsNotElementType():\r\n        try:\r\n            cat=el.Category\r\n            if cat is None:continue\r\n            if cat.CategoryType not in (CategoryType.Model,CategoryType.Annotation):continue\r\n            if el.IsHidden(view):continue\r\n            bb=el.get_BoundingBox(view)\r\n            if bb is None:continue\r\n            t=bb.Transform\r\n            for x in (bb.Min.X,bb.Max.X):\r\n                for y in (bb.Min.Y,bb.Max.Y):\r\n                    for z in (bb.Min.Z,bb.Max.Z):\r\n                        p=inverse.OfPoint(t.OfPoint(XYZ(x,y,z)))\r\n                        values.append(p.X)\r\n            ids.append(elem_num(el))\r\n        except Exception:\r\n            continue\r\n    if not values:raise ValueError('%s no model/annotation geometry available for crop trim'%view.Name)\r\n    return (min(values),max(values)),ids\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _try_trim_original_section_crop(view,cfg,scale,expected_model_ids=None,expected_annotation_ids=None):\r\n    \"\"\"Attempt to shorten original section line via ViewSection.CropBox width.\r\n\r\n    Optional/nonfatal API failure is reported, but model-content loss is always\r\n    fatal. Only CropBox X limits are changed; Y/Z/depth are untouched.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    result={'attempted':bool(cfg.get('original_marker_try_crop_trim',True)),\r\n            'status':'disabled','applied':False}\r\n    if not result['attempted']:return result\r\n    # Snapshot source-model element IDs for verification by caller as well.\r\n    try:\r\n        current=view.CropBox\r\n        extents,_=_crop_x_content_extents(view,cfg)\r\n        gap=mm_to_ft(float(cfg['original_marker_crop_padding_mm'])*scale)\r\n        min_width=mm_to_ft(float(cfg['original_marker_min_crop_width_mm'])*scale)\r\n        current_min=float(current.Min.X);current_max=float(current.Max.X)\r\n        old_width=current_max-current_min\r\n        if old_width<=0:raise ValueError('CropBox width <= 0')\r\n        proposed_min=max(current_min,extents[0]-gap)\r\n        proposed_max=min(current_max,extents[1]+gap)\r\n        if proposed_max<=proposed_min:\r\n            raise ValueError('Visible content has invalid crop X range')\r\n        # Keep at least 20 mm paper width centered on detected visible content.\r\n        if proposed_max-proposed_min<min_width:\r\n            center=.5*(proposed_min+proposed_max)\r\n            proposed_min=max(current_min,center-.5*min_width)\r\n            proposed_max=min(current_max,center+.5*min_width)\r\n        # Validate the INPUT fraction, not (1 - fraction). For the valid\r\n        # default 0.90, floating-point subtraction produces\r\n        # 0.09999999999999998, making the old >= 0.10 guard reject ALL scales.\r\n        max_shrink=float(cfg['original_marker_crop_max_shrink_fraction'])\r\n        if not math.isfinite(max_shrink) or not (0.0 <= max_shrink <= 0.90 + 1.0e-9):\r\n            raise ValueError('original_marker_crop_max_shrink_fraction must be within 0...0.90')\r\n        min_fraction=max(0.10, 1.0-min(max_shrink,0.90))\r\n        if proposed_max-proposed_min < min_fraction*old_width:\r\n            center=.5*(proposed_min+proposed_max)\r\n            h=.5*old_width*min_fraction\r\n            proposed_min=max(current_min,center-h)\r\n            proposed_max=min(current_max,center+h)\r\n            if proposed_max-proposed_min<2*h-1.0e-6:\r\n                # Preserve desired total crop width near a boundary.\r\n                proposed_min=max(current_min,proposed_max-2*h)\r\n                proposed_max=min(current_max,proposed_min+2*h)\r\n        old_mm=old_width*FT_TO_MM/float(scale)\r\n        new_mm=(proposed_max-proposed_min)*FT_TO_MM/float(scale)\r\n        result.update({'crop_width_before_mm':round(old_mm,2),\r\n                       'crop_width_requested_mm':round(new_mm,2),\r\n                       'source_visible_content_x_crop_ft':[round(extents[0],4),round(extents[1],4)]})\r\n        if new_mm>=old_mm-0.5:\r\n            result['status']='no_reduction_needed'\r\n            return result\r\n        subtx=SubTransaction(DOC)\r\n        subtx.Start()\r\n        try:\r\n            # Crop changes are OPTIONAL. A nested transaction allows clean\r\n            # rollback without losing the successful original marker move.\r\n            copybox=view.CropBox\r\n            copybox.Min=XYZ(proposed_min,copybox.Min.Y,copybox.Min.Z)\r\n            copybox.Max=XYZ(proposed_max,copybox.Max.Y,copybox.Max.Z)\r\n            view.CropBox=copybox\r\n            DOC.Regenerate()\r\n            newbox=view.CropBox\r\n            measured_mm=(newbox.Max.X-newbox.Min.X)*FT_TO_MM/float(scale)\r\n            if expected_model_ids is not None:\r\n                _,now_ids=model_bounds(view,cfg)\r\n                if (cfg.get('original_marker_require_source_model_ids_unchanged',True) and\r\n                        set(now_ids)!=set(expected_model_ids)):\r\n                    raise ValueError('crop trimmed away visible source MODEL elements')\r\n            if expected_annotation_ids is not None:\r\n                now_annotations=_visible_source_annotation_ids(view)\r\n                if (cfg.get('original_marker_require_source_annotations_unchanged',True) and\r\n                        set(now_annotations)!=set(expected_annotation_ids)):\r\n                    raise ValueError('crop trimmed away visible source ANNOTATIONS')\r\n            if measured_mm>=old_mm-0.5:\r\n                raise ValueError('Revit ignored source crop-width adjustment')\r\n            subtx.Commit()\r\n            result.update({'status':'cropped', 'applied':True,\r\n                           'crop_width_after_mm':round(measured_mm,2)})\r\n        except Exception as sub_exc:\r\n            # Revit might reject CropBox modifications on some view types, or\r\n            # the change may hide actual content. Keep marker movement only.\r\n            if subtx.GetStatus()==TransactionStatus.Started:\r\n                rolled=subtx.RollBack()\r\n                if rolled!=TransactionStatus.RolledBack:\r\n                    raise ValueError('Crop SubTransaction did not roll back')\r\n            result.update({'status':'crop_rejected_skipped', 'applied':False,\r\n                           'crop_rejection_reason':str(sub_exc)[:220],\r\n                           'crop_width_after_mm':round(old_mm,2)})\r\n        DOC.Regenerate()\r\n    except Exception as exc:\r\n        # Fail closed on unexpected projection/CropBox errors; the caller will\r\n        # roll back the complete trial instead of silently misrepresenting fit.\r\n        raise ValueError('Cannot safely trim %s section line: %s'%(view.Name,str(exc)[:270]))\r\n    return result\r\n\r\n\r\ndef reposition_original_markers_to_geometry(plan,records,geometry,cfg,scale):\r\n    \"\"\"Move true source cut markers alongside model, then trim line length.\r\n\r\n    Moving an ORIGINAL section shifts its section cut, not merely its symbol.\r\n    Before/after source model IDs must match unless explicitly opted out.\r\n    Caller owns a Revit trial/apply transaction. No independent transaction.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    if not cfg.get('original_marker_proximity',True):return {'status':'disabled','markers':[]}\r\n    if cfg.get('marker_strategy')!='original_direct_mirror':\r\n        return {'status':'not_applicable_reference_recreation','markers':[]}\r\n    if scale<=0:raise ValueError('Invalid scale')\r\n    gapx=float(cfg.get('original_marker_vertical_gap_mm',8.0))\r\n    gapy=float(cfg.get('original_marker_horizontal_gap_mm',8.0))\r\n    if not (2.0<=gapx<=35.0 and 2.0<=gapy<=35.0):\r\n        raise ValueError('Original marker model clearances must be 2...35 paper mm')\r\n    r=plan.RightDirection.Normalize();u=plan.UpDirection.Normalize()\r\n    before=_marker_plan_bounds(plan,records,geometry,scale)\r\n    result={'status':'evaluating','plan_marker_envelope_before':before,'markers':[]}\r\n    by_axis={rec['item']['axis']:rec for rec in records}\r\n    if set(by_axis)!=set(['vertical','horizontal']):\r\n        raise ValueError('Expected one vertical and one horizontal original marker')\r\n    for axis in ('vertical','horizontal'):\r\n        rec=by_axis[axis]\r\n        source=DOC.GetElement(rec['source'].Id)\r\n        marker=DOC.GetElement(rec['original'].Id)\r\n        if source is None or marker is None or marker.IsHidden(plan):\r\n            raise ValueError('Original %s marker missing/hidden during proximity step'%rec['name'])\r\n        # Important finding from the original-marker mirror probe: the\r\n        # associated source View.Origin can jump considerably even when the\r\n        # marker graphic barely moves. Anchor against the actual marker BBOX\r\n        # closest to the model, NOT source.Origin.\r\n        visible_marker=bounds_from_bb(marker.get_BoundingBox(plan),plan)\r\n        if visible_marker is None:raise ValueError('Original marker bbox missing for '+rec['name'])\r\n        if axis=='vertical':\r\n            nearest_edge=visible_marker.x1   # rightmost visible marker graphic\r\n            desired=geometry.x0-mm_to_ft(scale*gapx)\r\n            delta=desired-nearest_edge\r\n            vector=r.Multiply(delta)\r\n        else:\r\n            nearest_edge=visible_marker.y1   # uppermost visible marker graphic\r\n            desired=geometry.y0-mm_to_ft(scale*gapy)\r\n            delta=desired-nearest_edge\r\n            vector=u.Multiply(delta)\r\n        delta_mm=delta*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n        maxmove=float(cfg.get('original_marker_max_move_mm',165.0))\r\n        if abs(delta_mm)>maxmove:\r\n            raise ValueError('%s needs marker graphics displacement %.1fmm, over cap %.1fmm' %\r\n                             (rec['name'],delta_mm,maxmove))\r\n        _,ids_before=model_bounds(source,cfg)\r\n        ann_ids_before_move=_visible_source_annotation_ids(source)\r\n        pre_state=original_source_view_state(source)\r\n        did_move=abs(delta_mm)>float(cfg.get('original_marker_position_tolerance_mm',0.65))\r\n        if did_move:\r\n            ElementTransformUtils.MoveElement(DOC,marker.Id,vector)\r\n            DOC.Regenerate()\r\n        moved_source=DOC.GetElement(source.Id)\r\n        moved_marker=DOC.GetElement(marker.Id)\r\n        if moved_source is None or moved_marker is None or moved_marker.IsHidden(plan):\r\n            raise ValueError('%s source or original marker missing after MoveElement'%rec['name'])\r\n        moved_bounds=bounds_from_bb(moved_marker.get_BoundingBox(plan),plan)\r\n        if moved_bounds is None:raise ValueError('Marker bbox lost after MoveElement')\r\n        measured=((moved_bounds.x1 if axis=='vertical' else moved_bounds.y1)-desired)*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n        tolerance=float(cfg.get('original_marker_position_tolerance_mm',0.65))\r\n        if abs(measured)>tolerance:\r\n            raise ValueError('%s marker graphics did not move to desired position: %.2fmm error'%(\r\n                rec['name'],measured))\r\n        _,ids_after_move=model_bounds(moved_source,cfg)\r\n        annotation_ids_before=_visible_source_annotation_ids(moved_source)\r\n        if (cfg.get('original_marker_require_source_annotations_unchanged',True)\r\n                and set(annotation_ids_before)!=set(ann_ids_before_move)):\r\n            raise ValueError('%s lost/gained visible source annotations after MoveElement'%rec['name'])\r\n        if (cfg.get('original_marker_require_source_model_ids_unchanged',True)\r\n                and set(ids_before)!=set(ids_after_move)):\r\n            raise ValueError('%s lost/gained visible model elements after repositioning: %s => %s' %\r\n                             (rec['name'],ids_before[:15],ids_after_move[:15]))\r\n        crop_diag=_try_trim_original_section_crop(\r\n            moved_source,cfg,scale,expected_model_ids=ids_after_move,\r\n            expected_annotation_ids=annotation_ids_before)\r\n        # Some section crop edits also move the marker bubble/line graphics.\r\n        # Correct any such displacement using the marker bbox measured AFTER\r\n        # CropBox adjustment. Do not trust source Origin after mirroring.\r\n        final_marker_bounds=bounds_from_bb(marker.get_BoundingBox(plan),plan)\r\n        if final_marker_bounds is None:raise ValueError('%s marker bounds lost after crop trim'%rec['name'])\r\n        actual_edge=final_marker_bounds.x1 if axis=='vertical' else final_marker_bounds.y1\r\n        correction=desired-actual_edge\r\n        if abs(correction*FT_TO_MM/scale)>tolerance:\r\n            if abs(correction*FT_TO_MM/scale)>maxmove:\r\n                raise ValueError('%s crop changed marker edge too far to correct'%rec['name'])\r\n            ElementTransformUtils.MoveElement(DOC,marker.Id,\r\n                                               (r if axis=='vertical' else u).Multiply(correction))\r\n            DOC.Regenerate()\r\n        final_bounds=bounds_from_bb(marker.get_BoundingBox(plan),plan)\r\n        if final_bounds is None:raise ValueError('%s marker bounds missing after correction'%rec['name'])\r\n        final_gap=(geometry.x0-final_bounds.x1 if axis=='vertical'\r\n                   else geometry.y0-final_bounds.y1)*FT_TO_MM/scale\r\n        if abs(final_gap-(gapx if axis=='vertical' else gapy))>tolerance:\r\n            raise ValueError('%s actual marker-to-model clearance %.2fmm not within %.2fmm tolerance'%(\r\n                rec['name'],final_gap,tolerance))\r\n        _,ids_after=model_bounds(moved_source,cfg)\r\n        annotations_after=_visible_source_annotation_ids(moved_source)\r\n        if (cfg.get('original_marker_require_source_annotations_unchanged',True)\r\n                and set(annotations_after)!=set(annotation_ids_before)):\r\n            raise ValueError('%s changed source view annotation IDs during proximity'%rec['name'])\r\n        if (cfg.get('original_marker_require_source_model_ids_unchanged',True)\r\n                and set(ids_before)!=set(ids_after)):\r\n            raise ValueError('%s changed visible source elements after crop trim'%rec['name'])\r\n        result['markers'].append({\r\n            'view':rec['name'],'marker_id':elem_num(marker),'source_view_id':elem_num(source),\r\n            'axis':axis,'move_applied':did_move,\r\n            'requested_original_marker_graphic_shift_mm':round(delta_mm,2),\r\n            'measured_gap_from_plan_model_mm':round(final_gap,2),\r\n            'marker_position_error_before_crop_mm':round(measured,3),\r\n            'final_bbox_near_edge_model_ft':round(final_bounds.x1 if axis=='vertical' else final_bounds.y1,4),\r\n            'source_view_origin_before_xyz_ft':pre_state.get('origin'),\r\n            'source_view_origin_after_xyz_ft':original_source_view_state(moved_source).get('origin'),\r\n            'crop_trim':crop_diag,\r\n            'source_view_changes':sorted(k for k in set(pre_state)|set(original_source_view_state(moved_source))\r\n                                         if pre_state.get(k)!=original_source_view_state(moved_source).get(k)),\r\n            'source_model_ids_stable':set(ids_before)==set(ids_after),\r\n            'source_annotation_ids_stable':set(annotation_ids_before)==set(annotations_after),\r\n            'source_view_geometry_count_before':len(ids_before),'source_view_geometry_count_after':len(ids_after),\r\n            'source_cut_plane_moved':did_move,\r\n            'requires_visual_review':True})\r\n    DOC.Regenerate()\r\n    after=_marker_plan_bounds(plan,records,geometry,scale)\r\n    before_extent=before['extent_mm'];after_extent=after['extent_mm']\r\n    result.update({'status':'proximity_tested','plan_marker_envelope_after':after,\r\n                   'envelope_width_saved_mm':round(before_extent[0]-after_extent[0],2),\r\n                   'envelope_height_saved_mm':round(before_extent[1]-after_extent[1],2),\r\n                   'envelope_area_saved_mm2':round(before['area_mm2']-after['area_mm2'],2),\r\n                   'is_envelope_smaller':after['area_mm2']<before['area_mm2']})\r\n    return result\r\n\r\n\r\ndef perform_marker_strategy(plan,records,geometry,cfg,scale):\r\n    \"\"\"Use originals by default; retain proven v6.13 reference mode opt-in.\"\"\"\r\n    strategy=cfg.get('marker_strategy','original_direct_mirror')\r\n    if strategy=='reference_recreation_v613':\r\n        return perform_replacement(plan,records,geometry,cfg,scale)\r\n    if strategy!='original_direct_mirror':\r\n        raise ValueError('Unknown marker_strategy: '+str(strategy))\r\n    before_references=sorted(elem_num(id) for id in plan.GetReferenceSections())\r\n    plans=[]\r\n    for record in records:\r\n        old=record['original'];source=record['source'];axis=record['item']['axis']\r\n        if old is None or DOC.GetElement(old.Id) is None:\r\n            raise ValueError('Missing original marker '+record['name'])\r\n        if old.IsHidden(plan):\r\n            raise ValueError('Original marker %s hidden. Restore an initial sheet.'%record['name'])\r\n        if bool(old.Pinned):\r\n            raise ValueError('Original marker %s pinned; unpin in a backup first.'%record['name'])\r\n        do_mirror=(axis=='horizontal' and cfg.get('mirror_original_front',True) or\r\n                   axis=='vertical' and cfg.get('mirror_original_left',False))\r\n        do_mirror=(do_mirror and not cfg.get('skip_original_mirror',False))\r\n        if do_mirror and not ElementTransformUtils.CanMirrorElement(DOC,old.Id):\r\n            raise ValueError('Original %s marker cannot be mirrored'%record['name'])\r\n        # Snapshot pivot BEFORE editing any of the original marker/view objects.\r\n        pivot=original_marker_mirror_pivot(old,plan) if do_mirror else None\r\n        normal=((plan.RightDirection if axis=='horizontal' else plan.UpDirection).Normalize()\r\n                if do_mirror else None)\r\n        plans.append((record,do_mirror,pivot,normal))\r\n    data=[]\r\n    for record,do_mirror,pivot,normal in plans:\r\n        source=record['source'];old=record['original']\r\n        before=original_source_view_state(source)\r\n        source_id=elem_num(source);marker_id=elem_num(old)\r\n        if do_mirror:\r\n            one=List[ElementId]();one.Add(old.Id)\r\n            plane=Plane.CreateByNormalAndOrigin(normal,pivot)\r\n            copies=ElementTransformUtils.MirrorElements(DOC,one,plane,False)\r\n            if copies is not None and len(copies)>0:\r\n                raise ValueError('Original marker mirror unexpectedly returned copied elements')\r\n            DOC.Regenerate()\r\n        source_after=DOC.GetElement(source.Id)\r\n        marker_after=DOC.GetElement(old.Id)\r\n        if source_after is None or marker_after is None or elem_num(source_after)!=source_id:\r\n            raise ValueError('Source view / original marker lost during direct mirror')\r\n        if elem_num(marker_after)!=marker_id or marker_after.IsHidden(plan):\r\n            raise ValueError('Original marker changed ID or became hidden')\r\n        after=original_source_view_state(source_after)\r\n        changed=[key for key in sorted(set(before)|set(after)) if before.get(key)!=after.get(key)]\r\n        data.append({'name':record['name'],\r\n                     'original_marker_id':marker_id,\r\n                     'source_view_id':source_id,\r\n                     'mode':'mirror_original_in_place' if do_mirror else 'preserve_original_in_place',\r\n                     'create_references':False,\r\n                     'hide_originals':False,\r\n                     'mirror_pivot_xyz_ft':xyz_info(pivot) if pivot else None,\r\n                     'source_view_before':before,\r\n                     'source_view_after':after,\r\n                     'source_view_changed_fields':changed,\r\n                     'source_view_changes_detected':bool(changed),\r\n                     'requires_visual_QA':True})\r\n    # Proximity must run AFTER original mirror, since the mirror may move\r\n    # the cut-view origins. Original marker IDs are reused; no references built.\r\n    proximity=reposition_original_markers_to_geometry(plan,records,geometry,cfg,scale)\r\n    for item in data:\r\n        item['marker_proximity']=next((m for m in proximity.get('markers',[])\r\n                                      if m.get('view')==item['name']),None)\r\n    if data:\r\n        data[0]['plan_original_marker_envelope']=proximity\r\n    after_references=sorted(elem_num(id) for id in plan.GetReferenceSections())\r\n    if after_references!=before_references:\r\n        raise ValueError('Unexpected reference section list modification during original mirror')\r\n    return data\r\n\r\n\r\ndef align_original_elevation_titles(targets,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Ported from successful label-only v2: move only LabelOffset.X.\r\n\r\n    Always run AFTER general reanchoring, including after viewport placement.\r\n    Doesn't move the viewport center, source view, or original marker.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    if cfg.get('marker_strategy')!='original_direct_mirror' or not cfg.get('original_marker_title_alignment',True):\r\n        return {}\r\n    result={}\r\n    tolerance=float(cfg.get('geometry_title_tolerance_mm',1.25))\r\n    for key in cfg.get('align_elevation_titles_to_model',['front','left']):\r\n        if key not in ('front','left','plan'):\r\n            raise ValueError('Unsupported align_elevation_titles_to_model role: '+str(key))\r\n        vp,view=targets[key]\r\n        old_center=vp.GetBoxCenter();old_scale=int(view.Scale)\r\n        rect,details=model_geometry_sheet_rect((vp,view),cfg)\r\n        try:label=raw_outline(vp.GetLabelOutline())\r\n        except Exception:label=None\r\n        if label is None:\r\n            result[key]={'status':'no_title'}\r\n            continue\r\n        wanted=rect.x0-mm_to_ft(float(cfg['label_left_of_model_mm']))\r\n        dx=wanted-label.x0\r\n        distance_mm=dx*FT_TO_MM\r\n        if abs(distance_mm)>float(cfg['max_geometry_title_shift_mm']):\r\n            raise ValueError('%s title needs %.2fmm shift; exceeds max_geometry_title_shift_mm'%(\r\n                key,distance_mm))\r\n        old_y=label.y0\r\n        if abs(distance_mm)>.1:\r\n            offset=vp.LabelOffset\r\n            vp.LabelOffset=XYZ(offset.X+dx,offset.Y,offset.Z)\r\n            DOC.Regenerate()\r\n        after=raw_outline(vp.GetLabelOutline())\r\n        if after is None:raise ValueError('%s label outline missing after move'%key)\r\n        x_error=(after.x0-wanted)*FT_TO_MM\r\n        y_error=(after.y0-old_y)*FT_TO_MM\r\n        if abs(x_error)>tolerance or abs(y_error)>tolerance:\r\n            raise ValueError('%s title alignment failed: x %.2fmm, y drift %.2fmm'%(\r\n                key,x_error,y_error))\r\n        new_center=vp.GetBoxCenter()\r\n        if abs(new_center.X-old_center.X)>mm_to_ft(.02) or abs(new_center.Y-old_center.Y)>mm_to_ft(.02):\r\n            raise ValueError('%s viewport moved while ONLY its title was adjusted'%key)\r\n        if old_scale!=int(view.Scale):\r\n            raise ValueError('%s scale changed when moving title'%key)\r\n        result[key]={'status':'aligned' if abs(distance_mm)>.1 else 'already_aligned',\r\n                     'model_mm':rect.as_mm(),\r\n                     'title_before_mm':label.as_mm(),\r\n                     'title_after_mm':after.as_mm(),\r\n                     'label_x_shift_mm':round((after.x0-label.x0)*FT_TO_MM,2),\r\n                     'label_y_shift_mm':round((after.y0-label.y0)*FT_TO_MM,2),\r\n                     'left_error_mm':round(x_error,2)}\r\n    return result\r\n\r\n\r\ndef reanchor_titles_integrated(targets,cfg):\r\n    # The DIRECT mirror is intentionally allowed to change source view crops,\r\n    # but title-only operations must not do so. Mirror before title alignment.\r\n    capture=(cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='original_direct_mirror')\r\n    before={key:original_source_view_state(targets[key][1])\r\n            for key in ('front','left')} if capture else None\r\n    diag=reanchor_titles_after_replacement(targets,cfg)\r\n    diag['original_marker_geometry_title_alignment']=align_original_elevation_titles(targets,cfg)\r\n    if capture:\r\n        changes={key:[name for name in before[key] if before[key][name] !=\r\n                       original_source_view_state(targets[key][1]).get(name)]\r\n                 for key in before}\r\n        diag['source_view_changes_during_title_adjustments']=changes\r\n        if any(changes.values()):\r\n            raise ValueError('Viewport title adjustments unexpectedly changed source view(s): %s'%changes)\r\n    return diag\r\n\r\n\r\ndef other_view_marker_visibility(targets,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Manage only section marker elements referring to our four placed views.\r\n\r\n    Never hide view-specific tags or annotations merely because they share an\r\n    annotation category. The category and Name must BOTH match our criteria.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    view_names=set(str(v.Name).strip().lower() for vp,v in targets.values())\r\n    categories=set()\r\n    for name in ('OST_Viewers','OST_Sections','OST_ReferenceViewer'):\r\n        try:categories.add(enum_num(getattr(BuiltInCategory,name)))\r\n        except Exception:pass\r\n    report={}\r\n    for role in ('left','front','iso'):\r\n        vp,view=targets[role]\r\n        to_hide=List[ElementId]()\r\n        details=[]\r\n        for el in FilteredElementCollector(DOC,view.Id).WhereElementIsNotElementType():\r\n            try:\r\n                if el.Category is None or elem_num(el.Category.Id) not in categories:continue\r\n                if str(el.Name).strip().lower() not in view_names:continue\r\n                if el.IsHidden(view):continue\r\n                if not el.CanBeHidden(view):\r\n                    raise ValueError('Cannot hide marker %s in view %s'%(elem_num(el),view.Name))\r\n                to_hide.Add(el.Id)\r\n                details.append({'id':elem_num(el),'name':str(el.Name)})\r\n            except ValueError:raise\r\n            except Exception:continue\r\n        if to_hide.Count and cfg.get('hide_markers_outside_plan',True):\r\n            view.HideElements(to_hide)\r\n        report[role]={'found':details,\r\n                      'hidden_in_this_trial':bool(to_hide.Count and cfg.get('hide_markers_outside_plan',True))}\r\n    DOC.Regenerate()\r\n    return report\r\n\r\n\r\ndef get_sheet_rect(sheet):\r\n    o=sheet.Outline\r\n    return Rect(o.Min.U,o.Min.V,o.Max.U,o.Max.V)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef safe_area(sheet,cfg):\r\n    page=get_sheet_rect(sheet)\r\n    m=mm_to_ft(cfg['sheet_margin_mm'])\r\n    return Rect(page.x0+m, page.y0+max(m,cfg['reserved_bottom_fraction']*page.h),\r\n                page.x1-max(m,cfg['reserved_right_fraction']*page.w),\r\n                page.y1-m)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef obstacles(sheet,targets,cfg):\r\n    known=set(elem_num(vp) for vp,v in targets.values())\r\n    result=[];seen=set()\r\n    for vp_id in sheet.GetAllViewports():\r\n        if elem_num(vp_id) not in known:\r\n            vp=DOC.GetElement(vp_id)\r\n            result.append(('another viewport '+str(elem_num(vp)),viewport_footprint(vp)))\r\n    for element in FilteredElementCollector(DOC,sheet.Id).WhereElementIsNotElementType():\r\n        if isinstance(element,Viewport):continue\r\n        if isinstance(element,FamilyInstance):\r\n            try:\r\n                if element.Category and elem_num(element.Category.Id)==enum_num(BuiltInCategory.OST_TitleBlocks):\r\n                    continue\r\n            except Exception:pass\r\n        # Only sheet-owned elements, not annotations belonging to placed views.\r\n        try:\r\n            if element.ViewSpecific and elem_num(element.OwnerViewId)!=elem_num(sheet.Id):\r\n                continue\r\n        except Exception:pass\r\n        good=isinstance(element,(ScheduleSheetInstance,TextNote,FamilyInstance))\r\n        if not good:\r\n            try:\r\n                good=elem_num(element.Category.Id) in set(enum_num(x) for x in (\r\n                    BuiltInCategory.OST_GenericAnnotation,\r\n                    BuiltInCategory.OST_DetailComponents,\r\n                    BuiltInCategory.OST_RasterImages,\r\n                    BuiltInCategory.OST_RevisionClouds))\r\n            except Exception:pass\r\n        if not good:continue\r\n        if elem_num(element) in seen:continue\r\n        seen.add(elem_num(element))\r\n        try:bb=element.get_BoundingBox(sheet)\r\n        except Exception:bb=None\r\n        if bb is None:continue\r\n        values=(bb.Min.X,bb.Min.Y,bb.Max.X,bb.Max.Y)\r\n        if any(not math.isfinite(v) or abs(v)>10000 for v in values):continue\r\n        if bb.Max.X <= bb.Min.X or bb.Max.Y <= bb.Min.Y:continue\r\n        r=Rect(*values)\r\n        label=str(element.Name)\r\n        if isinstance(element,TextNote):\r\n            try:label += ' text='+repr(' '.join(str(element.Text).split())[:50])\r\n            except Exception:pass\r\n        result.append(('%s [id=%s]'%(label,elem_num(element)),r))\r\n    page=get_sheet_rect(sheet)\r\n    for i,data in enumerate(cfg['keepouts_normalized']):\r\n        if len(data)!=4:raise ValueError('keepouts_normalized must use 4 values per keepout')\r\n        x0,y0,x1,y1=[float(v) for v in data]\r\n        result.append(('manual keepout '+str(i+1),Rect(page.x0+page.w*x0,page.y0+page.h*y0,\r\n                                     page.x0+page.w*x1,page.y0+page.h*y1)))\r\n    return result\r\n\r\n\r\ndef title_adjust(vp,cfg):\r\n    box=viewport_box(vp)\r\n    try:\r\n        vp.LabelOffset=XYZ(0.0,-mm_to_ft(cfg['label_gap_mm']),0.0)\r\n        vp.LabelLineLength=min(mm_to_ft(cfg['label_line_mm']),max(mm_to_ft(22),box.w*0.45))\r\n    except Exception: pass  # Some viewports deliberately have no title.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\ndef model_geometry_sheet_rect(target,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Projected model-geometry bounds on the sheet for title anchoring.\r\n\r\n    Uses the visible model bounds in the target view and the Revit model->projection->sheet transforms.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    vp,view=target\r\n    bounds,model_ids=model_bounds(view,cfg)\r\n    transforms=view.GetModelToProjectionTransforms()\r\n    if transforms is None or len(transforms)!=1:\r\n        raise ValueError('Expected one model-to-projection transform for %s; split crops unsupported' % view.Name)\r\n    tr_model=transforms[0].GetModelToProjectionTransform()\r\n    tr_sheet=vp.GetProjectionToSheetTransform()\r\n    corners=[\r\n        view.Origin.Add(view.RightDirection.Multiply(bounds.x0)).Add(view.UpDirection.Multiply(bounds.y0)),\r\n        view.Origin.Add(view.RightDirection.Multiply(bounds.x0)).Add(view.UpDirection.Multiply(bounds.y1)),\r\n        view.Origin.Add(view.RightDirection.Multiply(bounds.x1)).Add(view.UpDirection.Multiply(bounds.y0)),\r\n        view.Origin.Add(view.RightDirection.Multiply(bounds.x1)).Add(view.UpDirection.Multiply(bounds.y1)),\r\n    ]\r\n    pts=[tr_sheet.OfPoint(tr_model.OfPoint(p)) for p in corners]\r\n    rect=Rect(min(p.X for p in pts),min(p.Y for p in pts),max(p.X for p in pts),max(p.Y for p in pts))\r\n    return rect,{'model_element_count':len(model_ids),'sheet_rect_mm':rect.as_mm()}\r\n\r\ndef project_view_rect_to_sheet(target,view_rect):\r\n    \"\"\"Map an element's view-coordinate bbox through actual Revit projection.\r\n\r\n    This is the same view -> sheet transform already used by model_geometry_sheet_rect.\r\n    The rect is expressed in view Right/Up axes, in model feet. Some original\r\n    references have large bboxes; they are INCLUDED if actually visible.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    vp,view=target\r\n    transforms=view.GetModelToProjectionTransforms()\r\n    if transforms is None or len(transforms)!=1:\r\n        raise ValueError('%s: content footprint requires a single model-to-projection transform'%view.Name)\r\n    m2p=transforms[0].GetModelToProjectionTransform()\r\n    p2s=vp.GetProjectionToSheetTransform()\r\n    points=[]\r\n    for x in (view_rect.x0,view_rect.x1):\r\n        for y in (view_rect.y0,view_rect.y1):\r\n            world=view.Origin.Add(view.RightDirection.Multiply(x)).Add(view.UpDirection.Multiply(y))\r\n            points.append(p2s.OfPoint(m2p.OfPoint(world)))\r\n    return Rect(min(pt.X for pt in points),min(pt.Y for pt in points),\r\n                max(pt.X for pt in points),max(pt.Y for pt in points))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef projected_view_content_footprint(target,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Printable-content envelope, NOT inflated viewport crop extents.\r\n\r\n    We include the model drawing, every visible annotation element in the view\r\n    (including the ORIGINAL section markers), and the viewport title. The\r\n    method is conservative; if a visible element cannot be projected, it raises\r\n    and the 1:25 candidate fails rather than ignoring possible collisions.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    vp,view=target\r\n    model,model_report=model_geometry_sheet_rect(target,cfg)\r\n    rects=[('model',model)]\r\n    collected=0;ids=[];failed=[];included=[]\r\n    for el in FilteredElementCollector(DOC,view.Id).WhereElementIsNotElementType():\r\n        try:\r\n            if el.Category is None:continue\r\n            # Model geometry is already represented by model_geometry_sheet_rect.\r\n            if el.Category.CategoryType==CategoryType.Model:continue\r\n            b=el.get_BoundingBox(view)\r\n            if b is None:continue\r\n            try:\r\n                if el.IsHidden(view):continue\r\n            except Exception:pass\r\n            r=bounds_from_bb(b,view)\r\n            if r is None or r.w<=0 or r.h<=0:continue\r\n            collected+=1\r\n            if collected>int(cfg.get('content_max_annotation_candidates',450)):\r\n                raise ValueError('%s annotation count exceeds limit; increase limit only after review'%view.Name)\r\n            sr=project_view_rect_to_sheet(target,r)\r\n            if sr.w<=0 or sr.h<=0:continue\r\n            rects.append(('annotation_'+str(elem_num(el)),sr))\r\n            included.append(elem_num(el))\r\n        except Exception as exc:\r\n            # With unreliable element projection, fail closed. A model view can\r\n            # have oversized section markers that we must not silently omit.\r\n            if cfg.get('fail_on_missing_view_content',True):\r\n                raise ValueError('%s: cannot project visible annotation %s: %s' % (\r\n                    view.Name,elem_num(el),str(exc)[:220]))\r\n            failed.append(str(exc)[:100])\r\n    # Keep the drawing envelope separate from the label so that an old label\r\n    # stranded by an oversized crop is NOT used as a geometry anchor.\r\n    drawing=Rect(min(r.x0 for name,r in rects),min(r.y0 for name,r in rects),\r\n                 max(r.x1 for name,r in rects),max(r.y1 for name,r in rects))\r\n    try:lab=raw_outline(vp.GetLabelOutline())\r\n    except Exception:lab=None\r\n    if lab is not None:rects.append(('title',lab))\r\n    if not rects:raise ValueError('%s has no measurable content'%view.Name)\r\n    bound=Rect(min(r.x0 for name,r in rects),min(r.y0 for name,r in rects),\r\n               max(r.x1 for name,r in rects),max(r.y1 for name,r in rects))\r\n    if bound.w*FT_TO_MM>1500 or bound.h*FT_TO_MM>1500:\r\n        raise ValueError('%s content footprint implausibly large (mm): %s'%(\r\n            view.Name,bound.size_mm()))\r\n    return bound,{'_printed_parts':rects,\r\n                  'model_mm':model.as_mm(),\r\n                  'annotation_count':collected,\r\n                  'annotation_ids_sample':included[:20],\r\n                  'visible_annotation_parts_mm':[\r\n                      {'element':key,'bbox_mm':r.as_mm()} for key,r in rects if key.startswith('annotation_')][:15],\r\n                  'drawing_only_bounds_mm':drawing.as_mm(),\r\n                  'drawing_only_rect':drawing,\r\n                  'view_title_mm':None if lab is None else lab.as_mm(),\r\n                  'raw_viewport_footprint_mm':viewport_footprint(vp).as_mm(),\r\n                  'measured_content_footprint_mm':bound.as_mm(),\r\n                  'annotation_projection_errors':failed[:4]}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef layout_footprints(targets,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Return rectangles + diagnostics for one consistent layout trial.\"\"\"\r\n    mode=str(cfg.get('_layout_footprint_basis','viewport'))\r\n    if mode=='viewport':\r\n        return ({key:viewport_footprint(vp) for key,(vp,view) in targets.items()},\r\n                {'mode':'viewport','measured_parts':{}})\r\n    if mode not in ('visible_content','sparse_content'):\r\n        raise ValueError('Unknown layout footprint basis '+mode)\r\n    result={};details={}\r\n    for key,target in targets.items():\r\n        rect,detail=projected_view_content_footprint(target,cfg)\r\n        rect=rect.expand(mm_to_ft(cfg.get('content_geometry_clearance_mm',2.0)))\r\n        result[key]=rect\r\n        # Rect is used only for in-transaction title placement, not for Watch.\r\n        details[key]={k:v for k,v in detail.items() if k not in ('drawing_only_rect','_printed_parts')}\r\n    return result,{'mode':'visible_content','measured_parts':details}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef sparse_parts_for_sheet(targets,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Capture every real printed part of each view separately in sheet coords.\r\n\r\n    Returns model geometry, individual visible annotation/reference marker\r\n    elements, AND the actual Viewport title outline. These parts can coexist\r\n    with another view's *empty* bounding-box area, but no printed parts may\r\n    collide. No marker/annotation is hidden, shortened or omitted here.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    result={}\r\n    for role,target in targets.items():\r\n        bound,report=projected_view_content_footprint(target,cfg)\r\n        parts=list(report['_printed_parts'])\r\n        cap=int(cfg.get('sparse_max_view_parts',80))\r\n        if len(parts)>cap:\r\n            raise ValueError('%s has %d visible content parts; cap %d, refusing approximate layout'%(\r\n                role,len(parts),cap))\r\n        if not any(name=='model' for name,rect in parts):\r\n            raise ValueError('%s missing actual model geometry in sparse fit'%role)\r\n        vp,view=target\r\n        ctr,_=model_geometry_sheet_center(target,cfg)\r\n        result[role]={'parts':parts,'bound':bound,'center':(ctr.X,ctr.Y),\r\n                      'model_part':next(rect for name,rect in parts if name=='model')}\r\n    return result\r\n\r\n\r\ndef sparse_collisions(parts_a,parts_b,clearance):\r\n    \"\"\"Pairwise PRINTED-content collisions, not full-envelope intersections.\"\"\"\r\n    for an,a in parts_a:\r\n        for bn,b in parts_b:\r\n            if a.expand(clearance).overlaps(b):\r\n                return '%s overlaps %s'%(an,bn)\r\n    return None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef sparse_translated(parts,dx,dy):\r\n    return [(name,r.move(dx,dy)) for name,r in parts]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef sparse_validation(placements,printable,occupied,clearance):\r\n    \"\"\"Check all moved printed elements against paper, fixed sheet content and peers.\"\"\"\r\n    for role,parts in placements.items():\r\n        for name,r in parts:\r\n            if not r.fits(printable):\r\n                return '%s %s outside printable sheet'% (role,name)\r\n            for obstacle_name,obstacle in occupied:\r\n                if r.expand(clearance).overlaps(obstacle):\r\n                    return '%s %s overlaps fixed sheet item %s'%(role,name,obstacle_name)\r\n    roles=list(placements)\r\n    for idx,role in enumerate(roles):\r\n        for other in roles[idx+1:]:\r\n            failure=sparse_collisions(placements[role],placements[other],clearance)\r\n            if failure:return '%s/%s %s'%(role,other,failure)\r\n    return None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef sparse_search(sparse,goals,printable,occupied,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Model-centered 2-row target with REAL element/marker collision testing.\r\n\r\n    The original max(topHeight)+max(planHeight) test is deliberately NOT used:\r\n    it assumes the Plan Detail's L-shaped section markers fill a solid rectangle.\r\n    The source cut views and markers are not modified, only viewport centers.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    c=mm_to_ft(float(cfg['obstacle_clearance_mm']))\r\n    limits={}\r\n    for role,info in sparse.items():\r\n        cx,cy=info['center'];b=info['bound']\r\n        limits[role]=(printable.x0 + (cx-b.x0),printable.x1 - (b.x1-cx),\r\n                      printable.y0 + (cy-b.y0),printable.y1 - (b.y1-cy))\r\n        xmin,xmax,ymin,ymax=limits[role]\r\n        if xmin>xmax or ymin>ymax:\r\n            return None,{'status':'no_fit', 'reason':'%s printed parts too large even for physical sheet'%role}\r\n    def span_axis(role1,role2,axis):\r\n        a=0 if axis=='x' else 2\r\n        return max(limits[role1][a],limits[role2][a]),min(limits[role1][a+1],limits[role2][a+1])\r\n    xmin,xmax=span_axis('front','plan','x')\r\n    tymin,tymax=span_axis('front','left','y')\r\n    bymin,bymax=span_axis('plan','iso','y')\r\n    if xmin>xmax or tymin>tymax or bymin>bymax:\r\n        return None,{'status':'no_fit','reason':'Aligned model centers cannot fit all printed parts inside page'}\r\n    n=max(5,min(13,int(cfg.get('sparse_candidate_samples',9))))\r\n    ns=max(3,min(11,int(cfg.get('sparse_secondary_samples',7))))\r\n    xs=sample_range(xmin,xmax,n,goals['front'][0])\r\n    tops=sample_range(tymin,tymax,n,goals['front'][1])\r\n    bottoms=sample_range(bymin,bymax,n,goals['plan'][1])\r\n    lefts=sample_range(limits['left'][0],limits['left'][1],ns,goals['left'][0])\r\n    isos=sample_range(limits['iso'][0],limits['iso'][1],ns,goals['iso'][0])\r\n    # Cache every tested per-view shifted component configuration. Each must\r\n    # avoid fixed notes / BOM / checklist, but other-view overlaps are checked\r\n    # only when combining four views.\r\n    valid_cache={}\r\n    def valid_parts(role,x,y):\r\n        ident=(role,x,y)\r\n        if ident in valid_cache:return valid_cache[ident]\r\n        info=sparse[role];cx,cy=info['center']\r\n        moved=sparse_translated(info['parts'],x-cx,y-cy)\r\n        for name,r in moved:\r\n            if not r.fits(printable):\r\n                valid_cache[ident]=None;return None\r\n            if any(r.expand(c).overlaps(obst) for _,obst in occupied):\r\n                valid_cache[ident]=None;return None\r\n        valid_cache[ident]=moved\r\n        return moved\r\n    best=None;best_score=None;attempts=0;near_misses=[]\r\n    max_trials=int(cfg.get('sparse_max_search_trials',65000))\r\n    # Determine model alignment / row targets; empty space between L arms is\r\n    # explicitly allowed. The first successful candidate can still be scored\r\n    # against normalized expected-layout goals to select the closest result.\r\n    for common_x in xs:\r\n        for top_y in tops:\r\n            front=valid_parts('front',common_x,top_y)\r\n            if front is None:continue\r\n            viable_lefts=[]\r\n            for left_x in lefts:\r\n                left=valid_parts('left',left_x,top_y)\r\n                if left is not None and not sparse_collisions(front,left,c):\r\n                    viable_lefts.append((left_x,left))\r\n            if not viable_lefts:continue\r\n            for bottom_y in bottoms:\r\n                plan=valid_parts('plan',common_x,bottom_y)\r\n                if plan is None:continue\r\n                if sparse_collisions(front,plan,c):continue\r\n                viable_isos=[]\r\n                for iso_x in isos:\r\n                    iso=valid_parts('iso',iso_x,bottom_y)\r\n                    if (iso is not None and not sparse_collisions(plan,iso,c)\r\n                            and not sparse_collisions(front,iso,c)):\r\n                        viable_isos.append((iso_x,iso))\r\n                if not viable_isos:continue\r\n                for left_x,left in viable_lefts:\r\n                    if sparse_collisions(left,plan,c):continue\r\n                    for iso_x,iso in viable_isos:\r\n                        attempts+=1\r\n                        if attempts>max_trials:break\r\n                        if sparse_collisions(left,iso,c):continue\r\n                        centers={'front':(common_x,top_y),'left':(left_x,top_y),\r\n                                 'plan':(common_x,bottom_y),'iso':(iso_x,bottom_y)}\r\n                        score=sum(float(cfg['layout_target_weights'].get(role,1.0)) *\r\n                                  ((xy[0]-goals[role][0])**2+(xy[1]-goals[role][1])**2)\r\n                                  for role,xy in centers.items())\r\n                        if best is None or score<best_score:\r\n                            best=centers;best_score=score\r\n                    if attempts>max_trials:break\r\n                if attempts>max_trials:break\r\n            if attempts>max_trials:break\r\n        if attempts>max_trials:break\r\n    return best,{'status':'fit' if best else 'no_fit','tested_valid_combinations':attempts,\r\n                 'cached_view_positions':len(valid_cache),'reason':None if best else\r\n                 'No element-level collision-free two-row target found at this scale',\r\n                 'search_exhausted':attempts>max_trials}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef check_layout_sparse(targets,available,occupied,cfg,bom_limit,page):\r\n    \"\"\"Find and VERIFY 1:25 using separate model, marker and title rectangles.\"\"\"\r\n    original_parts=sparse_parts_for_sheet(targets,cfg)\r\n    goals=layout_goals(page,cfg)\r\n    printed=page.expand(-mm_to_ft(cfg.get('sparse_printed_sheet_margin_mm',2.0)))\r\n    # Use ACTUAL paper outline, not the old footer rectangle: fixed sheet\r\n    # notes/QR/checklist/BOM are already represented by their own obstacles.\r\n    centers,diag=sparse_search(original_parts,goals,printed,occupied,cfg)\r\n    if centers is None:\r\n        return None,'Sparse 1:25 search: '+str(diag['reason'])\r\n    offsets={role:(centers[role][0]-info['center'][0],\r\n                   centers[role][1]-info['center'][1]) for role,info in original_parts.items()}\r\n    for role,(vp,view) in targets.items():\r\n        prior=vp.GetBoxCenter();dx,dy=offsets[role]\r\n        vp.SetBoxCenter(XYZ(prior.X+dx,prior.Y+dy,prior.Z))\r\n    DOC.Regenerate()\r\n    title_after=reanchor_titles_integrated(targets,cfg)\r\n    actual_parts=sparse_parts_for_sheet(targets,cfg)\r\n    real={role:info['parts'] for role,info in actual_parts.items()}\r\n    failure=sparse_validation(real,printed,occupied,mm_to_ft(cfg['obstacle_clearance_mm']))\r\n    if failure:return None,'Sparse post-move validation: '+failure\r\n    # Bounding rectangles CAN intersect but actual printed parts may not.\r\n    error=abs(actual_parts['front']['center'][0]-actual_parts['plan']['center'][0])*FT_TO_MM\r\n    if error>float(cfg['geometry_alignment_tolerance_mm']):\r\n        return None,'Sparse Front/Plan model center X difference %.2fmm'%error\r\n    # Preserve reference styling goals within tolerance; do not silently move\r\n    # outside the intended drawing zones to achieve a technically valid fit.\r\n    distances={role:round(math.hypot((info['center'][0]-goals[role][0])*FT_TO_MM,\r\n                                    (info['center'][1]-goals[role][1])*FT_TO_MM),2)\r\n               for role,info in actual_parts.items()}\r\n    largest=max(distances.values())\r\n    if largest>float(cfg.get('max_reference_center_error_mm',50)):\r\n        return None,'Sparse layout deviates %.2fmm from expected model center (limit %.1fmm)'%(\r\n            largest,float(cfg.get('max_reference_center_error_mm',50)))\r\n    return {'gap_mm':None,'layout_footprint_basis':'sparse_content',\r\n            'content_parts_checked':{role:len(info['parts']) for role,info in actual_parts.items()},\r\n            'sparse_search_diagnostics':diag,'distance_from_reference_mm':distances,\r\n            'target_model_centers_mm':{role:[round(v*FT_TO_MM,2) for v in xy]\r\n                                       for role,xy in goals.items()},\r\n            'predicted_model_centers_mm':{role:[round(v*FT_TO_MM,2) for v in info['center']]\r\n                                          for role,info in actual_parts.items()},\r\n            'front_plan_geometry_x_error_mm':round(error,3),\r\n            'geometry_title_alignment_after_placement':title_after.get(\r\n                'original_marker_geometry_title_alignment',{}),\r\n            'printable_sheet_mm':printed.as_mm(),\r\n            'title_outlines_mm':{role:raw_outline(vp.GetLabelOutline()).as_mm()\r\n                 for role,(vp,view) in targets.items()\r\n                 if raw_outline(vp.GetLabelOutline()) is not None},\r\n            'footprints_mm':{role:info['bound'].as_mm() for role,info in actual_parts.items()},\r\n            'allow_envelope_overlap_but_never_printed_overlap':True},None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef title_box_diagnostic(vp):\r\n    \"\"\"Raw label/box outlines, in sheet mm. Label footprint delta is not label height.\"\"\"\r\n    box=viewport_box(vp)\r\n    try: label=raw_outline(vp.GetLabelOutline())\r\n    except Exception: label=None\r\n    extra=viewport_footprint(vp)\r\n    data={'box_mm':box.as_mm(), 'box_size_mm':box.size_mm(),\r\n          'footprint_mm':extra.as_mm(), 'footprint_size_mm':extra.size_mm(),\r\n          'extra_below_box_mm':round(max(0.0,box.y0-extra.y0)*FT_TO_MM,2),\r\n          'extra_left_of_box_mm':round(max(0.0,box.x0-extra.x0)*FT_TO_MM,2),\r\n          'label_present':label is not None}\r\n    if label is not None:\r\n        data['label_mm']=label.as_mm()\r\n        data['label_size_mm']=label.size_mm()\r\n        data['label_top_gap_mm']=round((box.y0-label.y1)*FT_TO_MM,2)\r\n        data['label_left_gap_mm']=round((label.x0-box.x0)*FT_TO_MM,2)\r\n    try:\r\n        v=vp.LabelOffset\r\n        data['label_offset_mm']=[round(v.X*FT_TO_MM,2),round(v.Y*FT_TO_MM,2)]\r\n    except Exception as e:data['label_offset_error']=str(e)[:150]\r\n    return data\r\n\r\n\r\ndef reanchor_titles_after_replacement(targets,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"VERY IMPORTANT: marker replacement changes the BOX after the initial title placement.\r\n\r\n    Re-anchor actual title outlines to the measured NEW drawing box.\r\n    Delta is measured in sheet coordinates, not guessed from the original view size.\r\n    Only affects the viewport label, never the section geometry or source views.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    if not cfg.get('post_replacement_title_reanchor',True):\r\n        return {'disabled':True}\r\n    before={key:title_box_diagnostic(vp) for key,(vp,v) in targets.items()}\r\n    # Setting the title offset before marker replacement is not sufficient;\r\n    # Revit can keep the title's old sheet location as the viewport shrinks.\r\n    for key,(vp,v) in targets.items():title_adjust(vp,cfg)\r\n    DOC.Regenerate()\r\n    deltas={}\r\n    for key,(vp,v) in targets.items():\r\n        box=viewport_box(vp)\r\n        try:label=raw_outline(vp.GetLabelOutline())\r\n        except Exception:label=None\r\n        if label is None:\r\n            deltas[key]={'status':'no_label'}\r\n            continue\r\n        label_height=label.h*FT_TO_MM\r\n        if label_height>float(cfg.get('title_label_max_height_mm',45.0)):\r\n            raise ValueError('Viewport %s title itself has %.2f mm measured height. '\r\n                             'Cannot safely normalize this view title family.'%(key,label_height))\r\n        # For Plan Detail, anchor the view title to VISIBLE MODEL GEOMETRY, not\r\n        # the marker-inflated viewport box. This is the actual placement path:\r\n        # v6.4 still used `box.x0-label.x0`, so the Plan title stayed at far left.\r\n        # The Y anchor is below BOTH geometry and viewport graphics so the label\r\n        # cannot overlap section markers extending below the assembly.\r\n        anchor_name='viewport_box'\r\n        content_drawing=None\r\n        if cfg.get('_layout_footprint_basis','viewport') in ('visible_content','sparse_content'):\r\n            # In the adaptive 1:25 trial use only PRINTED model/marker content,\r\n            # not the old original section's inflated viewport crop, to locate\r\n            # titles vertically. The actual content collision check remains on.\r\n            _,content_report=projected_view_content_footprint((vp,v),cfg)\r\n            content_drawing=content_report['drawing_only_rect']\r\n        if key=='plan' and cfg.get('plan_title_anchor_to_geometry',True):\r\n            geometry_sheet,model_report=model_geometry_sheet_rect((vp,v),cfg)\r\n            offset_x=mm_to_ft(float(cfg.get('plan_title_from_geometry_offset_mm',-3.0)))\r\n            if cfg.get('title_align_mode_plan')=='geometry_center':\r\n                desired_left=geometry_sheet.cx+offset_x\r\n            else:\r\n                desired_left=geometry_sheet.x0+offset_x\r\n            desired_top=min(geometry_sheet.y0,\r\n                            content_drawing.y0 if content_drawing is not None else box.y0)-mm_to_ft(cfg['label_gap_mm'])\r\n            anchor_name='model_geometry'\r\n            geometry_target_mm=geometry_sheet.as_mm()\r\n        else:\r\n            desired_left=(content_drawing.x0 if content_drawing is not None else box.x0)\r\n            desired_top=(content_drawing.y0 if content_drawing is not None else box.y0)-mm_to_ft(cfg['label_gap_mm'])\r\n            if content_drawing is not None: anchor_name='visible_drawn_content'\r\n            geometry_target_mm=None\r\n        dx=desired_left-label.x0\r\n        dy=desired_top-label.y1\r\n        deltas[key]={\r\n            'status':'adjusted',\r\n            'anchor':anchor_name,\r\n            'geometry_on_sheet_mm':geometry_target_mm,\r\n            'target_title_left_mm':round(desired_left*FT_TO_MM,2),\r\n            'target_title_top_mm':round(desired_top*FT_TO_MM,2),\r\n            'delta_mm':[round(dx*FT_TO_MM,2),round(dy*FT_TO_MM,2)]}\r\n        if abs(dx)>mm_to_ft(.1) or abs(dy)>mm_to_ft(.1):\r\n            try:\r\n                offset=vp.LabelOffset\r\n                vp.LabelOffset=XYZ(offset.X+dx,offset.Y+dy,0)\r\n            except Exception as e:\r\n                raise ValueError('Unable to move %s viewport title after resizing: %s'%(key,str(e)[:220]))\r\n    DOC.Regenerate()\r\n    after={key:title_box_diagnostic(vp) for key,(vp,v) in targets.items()}\r\n    for key,item in after.items():\r\n        if not item['label_present']:continue\r\n        wanted=float(cfg['label_gap_mm'])\r\n        tolerance=float(cfg.get('title_reanchor_tolerance_mm',1.5))\r\n        measured=raw_outline(targets[key][0].GetLabelOutline())\r\n        target=deltas[key]\r\n        if measured is None:continue\r\n        actual_left=measured.x0*FT_TO_MM\r\n        actual_top=measured.y1*FT_TO_MM\r\n        left_error=actual_left-target['target_title_left_mm']\r\n        top_error=actual_top-target['target_title_top_mm']\r\n        target['actual_title_left_mm']=round(actual_left,2)\r\n        target['actual_title_top_mm']=round(actual_top,2)\r\n        target['anchor_left_error_mm']=round(left_error,2)\r\n        target['anchor_top_error_mm']=round(top_error,2)\r\n        if abs(left_error)>tolerance or abs(top_error)>tolerance:\r\n            raise ValueError('%s title failed to move to %s: X error %.2fmm, Y error %.2fmm. '\r\n                             'All edits rolled back.' % (key,target['anchor'],left_error,top_error))\r\n    return {'before':before,'delta':deltas,'after':after}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef relevant_sheet_obstacles(occupied,region,limit=25):\r\n    \"\"\"List fixed sheet items that intersect the usable area or its immediate edge.\"\"\"\r\n    margin=mm_to_ft(6)\r\n    data=[]\r\n    for name,r in occupied:\r\n        if r.overlaps(region.expand(margin)):\r\n            data.append({'name':name, 'bounds_mm':r.as_mm()})\r\n    data.sort(key=lambda d:(-d['bounds_mm'][3],d['bounds_mm'][0]))\r\n    return data[:limit]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef sample_range(lo,hi,n,pref=None):\r\n    if hi<lo-1e-8:return []\r\n    if hi<=lo:return [lo]\r\n    n=max(3,int(n))\r\n    data=[lo+(hi-lo)*i/(n-1) for i in range(n)]\r\n    if pref is None:pref=(lo+hi)/2.0\r\n    data.append(max(lo,min(hi,pref)))\r\n    return sorted(set(data),key=lambda x:(abs(x-pref),x))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef no_obstacle(r,available,occupied,clearance):\r\n    return r.fits(available) and not any(r.expand(clearance).overlaps(o) for name,o in occupied)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef model_geometry_sheet_center(target,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Real model center on the sheet (not viewport boundary or title center).\r\n\r\n    Revit 2024+ transforms View model space -> projection -> sheet space.\r\n    Refuse split crops rather than choosing an arbitrary transform.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    vp,view=target\r\n    bounds,model_ids=model_bounds(view,cfg)\r\n    transforms=view.GetModelToProjectionTransforms()\r\n    if transforms is None or len(transforms)!=1:\r\n        raise ValueError('Expected one model-to-projection transform for %s; split crops unsupported' % view.Name)\r\n    center_model=view.Origin.Add(view.RightDirection.Multiply(bounds.cx)).Add(\r\n        view.UpDirection.Multiply(bounds.cy))\r\n    projected=transforms[0].GetModelToProjectionTransform().OfPoint(center_model)\r\n    sheetpoint=vp.GetProjectionToSheetTransform().OfPoint(projected)\r\n    box=viewport_box(vp)\r\n    # Fail closed if computed geometry is inexplicably far outside its viewport box.\r\n    tolerance=mm_to_ft(6)\r\n    if not Rect(sheetpoint.X,sheetpoint.Y,sheetpoint.X,sheetpoint.Y).fits(box.expand(tolerance)):\r\n        raise ValueError('Model geometry center for %s projected outside viewport box; '\r\n                         'inspect crop/transforms' % view.Name)\r\n    return sheetpoint,{'model_center_ft':xyz_info(center_model),\r\n                       'sheet_center_mm':[round(sheetpoint.X*FT_TO_MM,2),\r\n                                          round(sheetpoint.Y*FT_TO_MM,2)],\r\n                       'model_element_count':len(model_ids)}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef detect_bom_keepout(sheet,occupied,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Protect top-right BOM from the very first header column, not reserved_right_fraction.\r\n\r\n    The example BOM begins at ~292.6 mm despite safe_area extending to 326.94 mm.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    page=get_sheet_rect(sheet)\r\n    override=cfg.get('bom_header_left_override_mm')\r\n    source='config_override'\r\n    if override is not None:\r\n        bom_x=page.x0+mm_to_ft(float(override))\r\n    else:\r\n        header_names=tuple(\"text='\"+str(x)+\"'\" for x in cfg['bom_header_detection_names'])\r\n        candidates=[]\r\n        for name,r in occupied:\r\n            if (any(h in name for h in header_names)\r\n                    and r.x0>page.x0+page.w*0.55\r\n                    and r.y1>page.y1-mm_to_ft(45)):\r\n                candidates.append((name,r))\r\n        if candidates:\r\n            bom_x=min(r.x0 for name,r in candidates)\r\n            source='detected_sheet_text'\r\n        else:\r\n            # Do not quietly claim dynamic detection if no header was found.\r\n            # Sample sheet's original BOM header begins at x~292.6 mm.\r\n            if str(sheet.SheetNumber)==str(cfg.get('sample_sheet_number_for_bom_fallback')):\r\n                bom_x=page.x0+mm_to_ft(292.0)\r\n                source='original_sample_sheet_only_fallback'\r\n            else:\r\n                raise ValueError('BOM headers not detected. Set bom_header_left_override_mm')\r\n    boundary=bom_x-mm_to_ft(float(cfg['bom_clearance_mm']))\r\n    top_band=page.y1-mm_to_ft(float(cfg['bom_keepout_top_band_mm']))\r\n    if boundary < page.x0 + page.w*0.45:\r\n        raise ValueError('Detected BOM keepout boundary implausibly far left; inspect config')\r\n    keepout=Rect(boundary,top_band,page.x1,page.y1)\r\n    return keepout,{'source':source,\r\n                    'bom_first_column_x_mm':round((bom_x-page.x0)*FT_TO_MM,2),\r\n                    'required_right_limit_mm':round((boundary-page.x0)*FT_TO_MM,2),\r\n                    'keepout_bounds_sheet_mm':keepout.as_mm()}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef left_first_range(lo,hi,n):\r\n    if hi<lo-1e-8:return []\r\n    if hi<=lo:return [lo]\r\n    n=max(3,int(n))\r\n    return [lo+(hi-lo)*i/(n-1) for i in range(n)]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef center_out_range(lo,hi,n):\r\n    if hi<lo-1e-8:return []\r\n    if hi<=lo:return [lo]\r\n    n=max(3,int(n))\r\n    vals=[lo+(hi-lo)*i/(n-1) for i in range(n)]\r\n    c=(lo+hi)*0.5\r\n    return sorted(vals,key=lambda v:(abs(v-c),v))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef layout_goals(page,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Targets from 1-result screenshot, as MODEL centers on the sheet.\r\n\r\n    Uses normalized full-sheet coordinates, not hardcoded pixels or the\r\n    initial view positions. The physical BOM / checklist can vary between sheets.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    targets=cfg.get('layout_model_center_targets',{})\r\n    values={}\r\n    for key in ('front','left','plan','iso'):\r\n        fractions=targets.get(key)\r\n        if not isinstance(fractions,(list,tuple)) or len(fractions)!=2:\r\n            raise ValueError('Missing normalized position for '+key)\r\n        fx,fy=float(fractions[0]),float(fractions[1])\r\n        if not (0<=fx<=1 and 0<=fy<=1):\r\n            raise ValueError('Normalized sheet targets must be within [0,1]')\r\n        values[key]=(page.x0+fx*page.w,page.y0+fy*page.h)\r\n    return values\r\n\r\n\r\ndef placement_score(sol,region,bom_limit,page=None,goals=None,geom_offsets=None,cfg=None):\r\n    \"\"\"Score a drawing arrangement by distance from the desired 1-result template.\r\n\r\n    No vertical scoring in v6.9 caused valid solutions to be arbitrarily\r\n    low on some sheets; this scores both axes from actual model geometry.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    if goals is not None:\r\n        weights=cfg.get('layout_target_weights',{})\r\n        total=0.0\r\n        for key,rect in sol.items():\r\n            offset=geom_offsets[key]\r\n            goal=goals[key]\r\n            dx=(rect.cx+offset[0]-goal[0])*FT_TO_MM\r\n            dy=(rect.cy+offset[1]-goal[1])*FT_TO_MM\r\n            # Both axes matter. A view 50 mm lower than the reference incurs\r\n            # far greater penalty than minor 2–3 mm horizontal offset.\r\n            total+=float(weights.get(key,1.0))*(dx*dx+dy*dy)\r\n        return -total\r\n    # Optional legacy comparison mode.\r\n    top_left=sol['front'].x0-region.x0\r\n    top_right=bom_limit-sol['left'].x1\r\n    bottom_left=sol['plan'].x0-region.x0\r\n    bottom_right=region.x1-sol['iso'].x1\r\n    top_gap=sol['left'].x0-sol['front'].x1\r\n    bottom_gap=sol['iso'].x0-sol['plan'].x1\r\n    span=(sol['left'].x1-sol['front'].x0)+(sol['iso'].x1-sol['plan'].x0)\r\n    return (-(abs(top_left-top_right)+abs(bottom_left-bottom_right))*2.0\r\n            + (top_gap+bottom_gap)*1.5 + span)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef layout_search(sizes,region,occupied,cfg,gap,geom_offsets,bom_limit,page):\r\n    \"\"\"Fit four views in a reference-aligned two-row grid.\r\n\r\n    Front+Plan model centers are X-aligned. Top row = Front & Left, bottom\r\n    row = Plan & 3D. The solver prefers actual model centers corresponding\r\n    to 1-result.png, but ALL placements still undergo collision checks.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    front,left,plan,iso=[sizes[k] for k in ('front','left','plan','iso')]\r\n    top_h=max(front.h,left.h);bottom_h=max(plan.h,iso.h)\r\n    if top_h+bottom_h+gap>region.h:\r\n        return None,'Top + bottom footprints exceed usable height'\r\n    clearance=mm_to_ft(float(cfg['obstacle_clearance_mm']))\r\n    n=max(9,min(33,int(cfg['elastic_samples'])))\r\n    foff=geom_offsets['front'][0];poff=geom_offsets['plan'][0]\r\n    xmin=max(region.x0+front.w*.5+foff,region.x0+plan.w*.5+poff)\r\n    xmax=min(region.x1-front.w*.5+foff,region.x1-plan.w*.5+poff,\r\n             bom_limit-front.w*.5+foff-gap-left.w,\r\n             region.x1-plan.w*.5+poff-gap-iso.w)\r\n    if xmax<xmin:\r\n        return None,'Front/Plan model X-aligned columns cannot fit left of BOM'\r\n    ymin=region.y0+bottom_h*.5\r\n    ymax=region.y1-top_h-gap-bottom_h*.5\r\n    if ymax<ymin:return None,'Rows do not fit vertically'\r\n\r\n    reference=(cfg.get('layout_mode','reference_1_result')=='reference_1_result')\r\n    goals=layout_goals(page,cfg) if reference else None\r\n    # Candidate row order follows the reference sheet rather than choosing\r\n    # the arbitrary middle of available vertical space.\r\n    if reference:\r\n        preferred_from_plan=goals['plan'][1]-geom_offsets['plan'][1]\r\n        preferred_from_front=(goals['front'][1]-geom_offsets['front'][1]\r\n                             -bottom_h*.5-gap-top_h*.5)\r\n        preferred_bottom=.55*preferred_from_plan+.45*preferred_from_front\r\n        bottom_candidates=sample_range(ymin,ymax,int(cfg['layout_target_candidate_rows']),preferred_bottom)\r\n        common_candidates=sample_range(xmin,xmax,n,goals['front'][0])\r\n    else:\r\n        bottom_candidates=center_out_range(ymin,ymax,13)\r\n        common_candidates=center_out_range(xmin,xmax,n)\r\n    best=None;best_score=None\r\n    for bottom_y in bottom_candidates:\r\n        top_y=bottom_y+bottom_h*.5+gap+top_h*.5\r\n        for common_x in common_candidates:\r\n            f=front.move(common_x-foff-front.cx,top_y-front.cy)\r\n            p=plan.move(common_x-poff-plan.cx,bottom_y-plan.cy)\r\n            if not no_obstacle(f,region,occupied,clearance):continue\r\n            if not no_obstacle(p,region,occupied,clearance):continue\r\n            if f.expand(clearance).overlaps(p):continue\r\n            lmin=f.x1+gap\r\n            lmax=min(bom_limit,region.x1)-left.w\r\n            imin=p.x1+gap\r\n            imax=region.x1-iso.w\r\n            if reference:\r\n                left_pref=goals['left'][0]-geom_offsets['left'][0]-left.w*.5\r\n                iso_pref=goals['iso'][0]-geom_offsets['iso'][0]-iso.w*.5\r\n                left_candidates=sample_range(lmin,lmax,n,left_pref)\r\n                iso_candidates=sample_range(imin,imax,n,iso_pref)\r\n            else:\r\n                left_candidates=center_out_range(lmin,lmax,n)\r\n                iso_candidates=center_out_range(imin,imax,n)\r\n            for left_x in left_candidates:\r\n                l=left.move(left_x-left.x0,top_y-left.cy)\r\n                if not no_obstacle(l,region,occupied,clearance):continue\r\n                if l.expand(clearance).overlaps(f) or l.expand(clearance).overlaps(p):continue\r\n                for iso_x in iso_candidates:\r\n                    i=iso.move(iso_x-iso.x0,bottom_y-iso.cy)\r\n                    if not no_obstacle(i,region,occupied,clearance):continue\r\n                    if any(i.expand(clearance).overlaps(rect) for rect in (f,p,l)):continue\r\n                    placed={'front':f,'left':l,'plan':p,'iso':i}\r\n                    score=placement_score(placed,region,bom_limit,page,goals,geom_offsets,cfg)\r\n                    if best is None or score>best_score:\r\n                        best=placed;best_score=score\r\n    if best is None:\r\n        return None,'No collision-free 1-result-style layout at this scale'\r\n    return best,None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef apply_positions(targets,sizes,placements):\r\n    for key,(vp,view) in targets.items():\r\n        cur=vp.GetBoxCenter()\r\n        old=sizes[key];new=placements[key]\r\n        vp.SetBoxCenter(XYZ(cur.X+new.cx-old.cx,cur.Y+new.cy-old.cy,0))\r\n    DOC.Regenerate()\r\n\r\n\r\ndef check_layout(targets,available,occupied,cfg,bom_limit,page):\r\n    if cfg.get('_layout_footprint_basis')=='sparse_content':\r\n        return check_layout_sparse(targets,available,occupied,cfg,bom_limit,page)\r\n    gaps=[cfg['gap_mm'],max(cfg['minimum_gap_mm'],cfg['gap_mm']*.75),cfg['minimum_gap_mm']]\r\n    last_error='No geometry-aligned position found'\r\n    # Derive per-viewport geometry offset once per gap, after the marker and title changes.\r\n    for gap_mm in sorted(set(float(g) for g in gaps),reverse=True):\r\n        sizes,footprint_report=layout_footprints(targets,cfg)\r\n        center_p,report_p=model_geometry_sheet_center(targets['plan'],cfg)\r\n        center_f,report_f=model_geometry_sheet_center(targets['front'],cfg)\r\n        offsets={'plan':(center_p.X-sizes['plan'].cx,\r\n                         center_p.Y-sizes['plan'].cy),\r\n                 'front':(center_f.X-sizes['front'].cx,\r\n                          center_f.Y-sizes['front'].cy)}\r\n        # Left/3D model transforms may vary by view crop or version; anchor\r\n        # to their model center when available, otherwise the viewport center.\r\n        center_sources={'front':'model','plan':'model'}\r\n        for key in ('left','iso'):\r\n            try:\r\n                ctr,_=model_geometry_sheet_center(targets[key],cfg)\r\n                offsets[key]=(ctr.X-sizes[key].cx,ctr.Y-sizes[key].cy)\r\n                center_sources[key]='model'\r\n            except Exception:\r\n                offsets[key]=(0.0,0.0)\r\n                center_sources[key]='viewport_fallback'\r\n        solution,reason=layout_search(sizes,available,occupied,cfg,\r\n                                      mm_to_ft(gap_mm),offsets,bom_limit,page)\r\n        if solution is None:\r\n            last_error=reason;continue\r\n        apply_positions(targets,sizes,solution)\r\n        # Revit may update LabelOffset when moving viewports; normalize again\r\n        # after final placement before measuring collisions and committing.\r\n        post_layout_titles=reanchor_titles_integrated(targets,cfg)\r\n        actual,actual_footprint_report=layout_footprints(targets,cfg)\r\n        clr=mm_to_ft(cfg['obstacle_clearance_mm'])\r\n        errors=[]\r\n        # Explicitly check print-sheet bounds: on the failing 2-result,\r\n        # Plan Detail's title was BELOW the bottom sheet border.\r\n        printed=page.expand(-mm_to_ft(float(cfg['title_page_clearance_mm'])))\r\n        title_bounds={}\r\n        for key,(vp,view) in targets.items():\r\n            try:label=raw_outline(vp.GetLabelOutline())\r\n            except Exception:label=None\r\n            if label is not None:\r\n                title_bounds[key]=label.as_mm()\r\n                if not label.fits(printed):\r\n                    errors.append('%s title outside printable page by %.1fmm clearance'%(\r\n                        key,float(cfg['title_page_clearance_mm'])))\r\n        for key,rect in actual.items():\r\n            if not no_obstacle(rect,available,occupied,clr):\r\n                errors.append('%s touches sheet keepout' % key)\r\n        for a in actual:\r\n            for b in actual:\r\n                if a>=b:continue\r\n                if actual[a].expand(clr).overlaps(actual[b]):\r\n                    errors.append('%s and %s overlap'%(a,b))\r\n        if actual['left'].x1>bom_limit+mm_to_ft(0.1):\r\n            errors.append('Elevation Left extends into BOM hard limit')\r\n        center_plan,info_plan=model_geometry_sheet_center(targets['plan'],cfg)\r\n        center_front,info_front=model_geometry_sheet_center(targets['front'],cfg)\r\n        error_mm=abs(center_plan.X-center_front.X)*FT_TO_MM\r\n        if error_mm>float(cfg['geometry_alignment_tolerance_mm']):\r\n            errors.append('Front/Plan geometry X misaligned by %.2f mm' % error_mm)\r\n        if not errors:\r\n            model_anchor_mm={}\r\n            for key,rect in actual.items():\r\n                if center_sources[key]=='model':\r\n                    # Measured AFTER placement, not derived from the old\r\n                    # viewport footprint (which may change with title offsets).\r\n                    ctr,_=model_geometry_sheet_center(targets[key],cfg)\r\n                    model_anchor_mm[key]=[round(ctr.X*FT_TO_MM,2),\r\n                                          round(ctr.Y*FT_TO_MM,2)]\r\n                else:\r\n                    model_anchor_mm[key]=[round((rect.cx+offsets[key][0])*FT_TO_MM,2),\r\n                                          round((rect.cy+offsets[key][1])*FT_TO_MM,2)]\r\n            if cfg.get('layout_mode','reference_1_result')=='reference_1_result':\r\n                goals=layout_goals(page,cfg)\r\n                target_errors={key:round(math.hypot(model_anchor_mm[key][0]-gx*FT_TO_MM,\r\n                                                    model_anchor_mm[key][1]-gy*FT_TO_MM),2)\r\n                               for key,(gx,gy) in goals.items()}\r\n                biggest=max(target_errors.values())\r\n                if biggest>float(cfg.get('max_reference_center_error_mm',40.0)):\r\n                    last_error=('Closest safe result is too far from reference image: '\r\n                                'worst model-center deviation %.1fmm; per view %s' %\r\n                                (biggest,str(target_errors)))\r\n                    continue\r\n            else:\r\n                target_errors={}\r\n            return {'gap_mm':gap_mm,\r\n                    'layout_footprint_basis':cfg.get('_layout_footprint_basis','viewport'),\r\n                    'content_footprint_diagnostics':actual_footprint_report,\r\n                    'distance_from_reference_mm':target_errors,\r\n                    'layout_mode':cfg.get('layout_mode','reference_1_result'),\r\n                    'model_center_anchor_sources':center_sources,\r\n                    'target_model_centers_mm':{k:[round(v*FT_TO_MM,2) for v in pos]\r\n                                               for k,pos in layout_goals(page,cfg).items()},\r\n                    'predicted_model_centers_mm':model_anchor_mm,\r\n                    'title_outlines_mm':title_bounds,\r\n                    'geometry_title_alignment_after_placement':post_layout_titles.get(\r\n                        'original_marker_geometry_title_alignment',{}),\r\n                    'footprints_mm':{k:r.as_mm() for k,r in actual.items()},\r\n                    'geometry_centers_sheet_mm':{'plan':info_plan['sheet_center_mm'],\r\n                                                  'front':info_front['sheet_center_mm']},\r\n                    'front_plan_geometry_x_error_mm':round(error_mm,3),\r\n                    'elevation_left_right_mm':round(actual['left'].x1*FT_TO_MM,2),\r\n                    'bom_hard_right_limit_mm':round(bom_limit*FT_TO_MM,2)},None\r\n        last_error='Post-move validation: '+', '.join(errors)\r\n    return None,last_error\r\n\r\ndef scale_trials_order(cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"A smaller denominator = a larger drawing, chosen ONLY if it fits.\"\"\"\r\n    forced=cfg.get('force_scale')\r\n    if forced is not None:\r\n        values=[int(forced)]\r\n    elif cfg.get('scale_selection_mode','largest_fit')=='largest_fit':\r\n        values=sorted(set(int(v) for v in cfg.get('scale_candidates',[25,50,75,100])))\r\n    else:\r\n        preferred=int(cfg['preferred_scale'])\r\n        values=[preferred]+[int(v) for v in cfg['fallback_scales'] if int(v)!=preferred]\r\n    if not values or any(v<=0 or v>1000 for v in values):\r\n        raise ValueError('Invalid candidate view scales')\r\n    return list(dict.fromkeys(values))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef apply_scale(targets,scale,cfg):\r\n    for key,(vp,v) in targets.items():\r\n        if key=='iso' and v.ViewType==ViewType.ThreeD and v.IsPerspective:\r\n            raise ValueError('Perspective 3D view cannot share target scale')\r\n        if int(v.Scale)!=scale:v.Scale=scale\r\n    DOC.Regenerate()\r\n    for key,(vp,v) in targets.items():\r\n        if int(v.Scale)!=scale:\r\n            raise ValueError('Scale failed to change for %s, possibly view-template controlled'%v.Name)\r\n        title_adjust(vp,cfg)\r\n    DOC.Regenerate()\r\n\r\n\r\ndef marker_search_profiles(cfg,preferred=True):\r\n    \"\"\"First preserve 100% geometry height, then modestly adjust percentage/title gap.\"\"\"\r\n    label_gaps=list(dict.fromkeys([float(cfg['label_gap_mm'])]+list(\r\n        float(x) for x in cfg.get('search_label_gap_mm',[5,3,2]))))\r\n    if not preferred:label_gaps=label_gaps[:1]\r\n    ratios=list(dict.fromkeys(float(v) for v in cfg['vertical_height_ratios']))\r\n    if not preferred:ratios=ratios[:1]\r\n    output=[]\r\n    for ratio in ratios:\r\n        for gap in label_gaps:\r\n            output.append({'name':'geometry_%.2f_label_%gmm'%(ratio,gap),\r\n                           'height_ratio':ratio,'label_gap_mm':gap})\r\n    return output[:int(cfg['max_marker_profiles'])]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef profile_configuration(cfg,profile):\r\n    local=dict(cfg)\r\n    local['vertical_marker_height_ratio']=float(profile['height_ratio'])\r\n    local['label_gap_mm']=float(profile['label_gap_mm'])\r\n    return local\r\n\r\ndef preferred_layout_height_diagnostic(targets,region,cfg):\r\n    rectangles,measured=layout_footprints(targets,cfg)\r\n    heights={k:round(rectangles[k].h*FT_TO_MM,2) for k in rectangles}\r\n    needed=max(heights['front'],heights['left'])+max(heights['plan'],heights['iso'])+float(cfg['minimum_gap_mm'])\r\n    available=region.h*FT_TO_MM\r\n    return {'layout_footprint_basis':cfg.get('_layout_footprint_basis','viewport'),\r\n            'component_heights_mm':heights,\r\n            'row_height_lower_bound_mm':round(needed,2),\r\n            'available_height_mm':round(available,2),\r\n            'row_height_shortfall_mm':round(max(0.0,needed-available),2),\r\n            'is_conclusive':cfg.get('_layout_footprint_basis','viewport')!='sparse_content',\r\n            'note':'Envelope shortfall is not a rejection criterion for sparse_content'\r\n                   if cfg.get('_layout_footprint_basis')=='sparse_content' else None}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef evaluate_profile(sheet,targets,records,geometry,available,fixed_with_bom,bom_limit,cfg,scale,profile):\r\n    \"\"\"Every candidate gets its own Revit transaction, rolled back on exit.\"\"\"\r\n    local=profile_configuration(cfg,profile)\r\n    candidate_records=[]\r\n    for record,item in zip(records,local['references']):\r\n        newrecord=dict(record)\r\n        newrecord['item']=item\r\n        candidate_records.append(newrecord)\r\n    tx=Transaction(DOC,'TEMP v6.18.2 X-cut, original mirror and layout - 1:%s %s'%(scale,profile['name']))\r\n    tx.Start()\r\n    summary={'profile':profile['name'],'vertical_height_ratio':profile['height_ratio'],\r\n             'label_gap_mm':profile['label_gap_mm'],'status':'unknown'}\r\n    try:\r\n        apply_scale(targets,scale,local)\r\n        planvp,plan=targets['plan']\r\n        before=viewport_footprint(planvp).size_mm()\r\n        x_diags=try_elevation_left_x_with_subtransaction(targets,local,scale)\r\n        summary['hidden_x_adjustment']=x_diags\r\n        live_geometry,_=model_bounds(plan,local)\r\n        created=perform_marker_strategy(plan,candidate_records,live_geometry,local,scale)\r\n        if local.get('marker_strategy')=='original_direct_mirror':\r\n            # No visibility operations on other views. This mode reuses originals.\r\n            others={key:{'found':[],'hidden_in_this_trial':False}\r\n                    for key in ('front','left','iso')}\r\n        else:\r\n            others=other_view_marker_visibility(targets,local)\r\n        title_diagnostics=reanchor_titles_integrated(targets,local)\r\n        summary['geometry_elevation_title_realign']=title_diagnostics.get(\r\n            'original_marker_geometry_title_alignment',{})\r\n        summary['title_reanchor_mm']={\r\n            key:{'move_mm':title_diagnostics['delta'][key].get('delta_mm'),\r\n                 'anchor':title_diagnostics['delta'][key].get('anchor'),\r\n                 'target_title_left_mm':title_diagnostics['delta'][key].get('target_title_left_mm'),\r\n                 'actual_title_left_mm':title_diagnostics['delta'][key].get('actual_title_left_mm'),\r\n                 'anchor_left_error_mm':title_diagnostics['delta'][key].get('anchor_left_error_mm'),\r\n                 'geometry_on_sheet_mm':title_diagnostics['delta'][key].get('geometry_on_sheet_mm'),\r\n                 'measured_gap_mm':title_diagnostics['after'][key].get('label_top_gap_mm'),\r\n                 'extra_below_box_mm':title_diagnostics['after'][key]['extra_below_box_mm']}\r\n            for key in targets}\r\n        summary['plan_title_outline_mm']={\r\n            'before':title_diagnostics['before']['plan'],\r\n            'after':title_diagnostics['after']['plan']}\r\n        if not local.get('hide_markers_outside_plan',True) and any(\r\n                others[k]['found'] for k in ('front','left','iso')):\r\n            raise ValueError('Visible section markers outside Plan Detail')\r\n        after=viewport_footprint(planvp).size_mm()\r\n        summary['plan_footprint_before_mm']=before\r\n        summary['plan_footprint_after_mm']=after\r\n        summary['layout_footprint_basis']=local.get('_layout_footprint_basis','viewport')\r\n        summary['plan_viewport_box_after_mm']=viewport_box(planvp).size_mm()\r\n        summary['plan_label_extra_height_mm']=round(after[1]-summary['plan_viewport_box_after_mm'][1],2)  # extra extent, NOT title glyph height\r\n        summary['saved_plan_height_mm']=round(before[1]-after[1],2)\r\n        summary['saved_plan_width_mm']=round(before[0]-after[0],2)\r\n        summary['height_feasibility']=preferred_layout_height_diagnostic(targets,available,local)\r\n        summary['reference_diagnostics']=created\r\n        summary['plan_marker_proximity_diagnostics']=next(\r\n            (d.get('plan_original_marker_envelope') for d in created\r\n             if d.get('plan_original_marker_envelope') is not None),None)\r\n        summary['marker_visibility_other_views']=others\r\n        if (not local.get('scale_selection_mode')=='largest_fit' and\r\n                scale==int(local['preferred_scale']) and\r\n                summary['saved_plan_height_mm'] < float(local['min_height_saving_paper_mm']) and\r\n                local.get('marker_strategy')!='original_direct_mirror'):\r\n            summary['status']='no_fit'\r\n            summary['reason']='Replacement increases Plan Detail height'\r\n        elif (local.get('_layout_footprint_basis')!='sparse_content' and\r\n              summary['height_feasibility']['row_height_shortfall_mm']>0):\r\n            summary['status']='no_fit'\r\n            summary['reason']='Plan plus upper elevation row exceeds usable sheet height'\r\n        else:\r\n            solution,reason=check_layout(targets,available,fixed_with_bom,local,bom_limit,get_sheet_rect(sheet))\r\n            if solution is None:\r\n                summary['status']='no_fit'; summary['reason']=reason\r\n            else:\r\n                summary['status']='fit'; summary['layout']=solution\r\n    except Exception as exc:\r\n        summary['status']='error'\r\n        summary['reason']=str(exc)[:850]\r\n    finally:\r\n        rollback=tx.RollBack()\r\n        if rollback!=TransactionStatus.RolledBack:\r\n            raise RuntimeError('Marker trial failed to roll back; inspect Revit before continuing')\r\n    return summary\r\n\r\n\r\ndef selected_sheet_policy(sheet,cfg):\r\n    \"\"\"Select exactly IN[0]'s ViewSheet or the current active ViewSheet.\r\n\r\n    No sheet ID from another Revit model is silently substituted. Optional\r\n    expected_sheet_number is a safety lock, not a required global setting.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    actual=str(sheet.SheetNumber).strip()\r\n    requested=cfg.get('expected_sheet_number')\r\n    requested=str(requested).strip() if requested is not None else None\r\n    policy={\r\n        'mode':'explicit_sheet_number_lock' if requested else 'active_or_supplied_ViewSheet',\r\n        'actual_sheet_number':actual,\r\n        'expected_sheet_number':requested,\r\n        'passed':bool(actual) and (not requested or actual==requested),\r\n    }\r\n    if not actual:\r\n        return policy,'Active ViewSheet has an empty sheet number; refuse to modify it'\r\n    if requested and actual!=requested:\r\n        return policy,'The selected sheet number does not match optional expected_sheet_number: %s vs %s' % (\r\n            actual,requested)\r\n    return policy,None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef run_sheet(sheet,cfg,dry_run):\r\n    result={'sheet':str(sheet.SheetNumber),'status':'error',\r\n        'dry_run':dry_run,'reference_preview':[], 'scale_trials':[],\r\n        'warnings':[], 'selected_scale':None,'selected_gap_mm':None,\r\n        'selected_marker_profile':None,'committed':False,\r\n        'original_marker_strategy':cfg.get('marker_strategy'),\r\n        'reference_markers_created':0 if cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='original_direct_mirror' else None,\r\n        'original_markers_hidden':0 if cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='original_direct_mirror' else None,\r\n        'mirror_is_skipped':bool(cfg.get('skip_original_mirror',False)),\r\n        'explanation':'v6.18.2: hidden original X/Plan Detail cutting marker moved above full assembly in Elevation Left; original marker geometry proximity, direct front mirror, 1:25-first adaptive sparse layout, titles and BOM protection retained'}\r\n    result['sheet_selection'],selection_error=selected_sheet_policy(sheet,cfg)\r\n    if selection_error:\r\n        result['error']=selection_error\r\n        return result\r\n    targets=get_targets(sheet,cfg)\r\n    planvp,plan=targets['plan']\r\n    records=validate_reference_sources(plan,cfg['references'],targets)\r\n    result['resolved_references']=[r['resolution'] for r in records]\r\n    # Preflight once, outside trials, so we do not collect document-wide hidden\r\n    # markers 15+ times while exploring 1:25 layout profiles. Source/candidate\r\n    # IDs are model-specific and NEVER hard-coded as standard defaults.\r\n    if cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_to_top',True):\r\n        try:\r\n            spatial=_assembly_spatial_bounds_for_x(plan,targets['left'][1],cfg)\r\n            cfg['_x_assembly_spatial']=spatial\r\n            marker,diag=_x_resolve_hidden_marker(targets['left'][1],plan,cfg,spatial)\r\n            result['elevation_left_hidden_x_preflight']=diag\r\n            if marker is not None:\r\n                cfg['_resolved_x_marker_id']=elem_num(marker)\r\n                result['elevation_left_hidden_x_preflight']['selected_id']=elem_num(marker)\r\n            else:\r\n                cfg['_x_marker_preflight_missing']=diag\r\n                result['warnings'].append('Hidden Elevation Left X marker not uniquely identified; '+\r\n                                          'inspect automatic discovery diagnostics.')\r\n                if cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_missing_policy','error')=='error':\r\n                    raise ValueError('Cannot identify original hidden X marker. '+str(diag)[:850])\r\n        except Exception as exc:\r\n            diagnostic={'status':'preflight_error','reason':str(exc)[:450]}\r\n            result['elevation_left_hidden_x_preflight']=diagnostic\r\n            if cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_missing_policy')=='error':\r\n                raise\r\n            cfg['_x_marker_preflight_missing']=diagnostic\r\n            result['warnings'].append('Hidden X marker preflight skipped: '+str(exc)[:180])\r\n    else:\r\n        result['elevation_left_hidden_x_preflight']={'status':'disabled'}\r\n    for k,(vp,_) in targets.items():\r\n        if vp.Pinned:raise ValueError('Pinned viewport %s; unpin before running'%k)\r\n    if cfg['gap_mm']<cfg['minimum_gap_mm'] or cfg['minimum_gap_mm']<1:\r\n        raise ValueError('Require gap_mm >= minimum_gap_mm >= 1')\r\n    geometry,model_ids=model_bounds(plan,cfg)\r\n    result['assembly_model_element_count']=len(model_ids)\r\n    result['assembly_bounds_in_plan_model_ft']=[round(v,3) for v in\r\n                                                (geometry.x0,geometry.y0,geometry.x1,geometry.y1)]\r\n    result['original_plan_viewport_box_mm']=viewport_box(planvp).size_mm()\r\n    result['starting_view_measurements']={\r\n        k:{'view_id':elem_num(v),'scale':int(v.Scale),\r\n           'viewport_box_mm':viewport_box(vp).size_mm(),\r\n           'viewport_plus_label_mm':viewport_footprint(vp).size_mm()}\r\n        for k,(vp,v) in targets.items()}\r\n    available=safe_area(sheet,cfg)\r\n    result['usable_sheet_region_mm']=available.as_mm()\r\n    fixed=obstacles(sheet,targets,cfg)\r\n    result['fixed_obstacle_count']=len(fixed)\r\n    bom_keepout,bom_report=detect_bom_keepout(sheet,fixed,cfg)\r\n    bom_limit=bom_keepout.x0\r\n    fixed_with_bom=fixed+[('HARD BOM EXCLUSION',bom_keepout)]\r\n    result['bom_protection']=bom_report\r\n    result['nearby_fixed_obstacles']=relevant_sheet_obstacles(fixed,available)\r\n    result['marker_visibility_other_views']={}\r\n    result['elevation_left_x_feature_enabled']=bool(cfg.get('elevation_left_hidden_x_to_top',True))\r\n    if not dry_run:\r\n        result['warnings'].append('FULL SHEET APPLY on backup only: all layout and source-view checks must pass.')\r\n    winning=None\r\n    # Try 1:25 first by default; choose the first FULLY FITTING scale.\r\n    # 1:50 is a useful baseline but no longer an enforced scale.\r\n    ordered_scales=scale_trials_order(cfg)\r\n    result['scale_selection_policy']={'mode':cfg.get('scale_selection_mode','largest_fit'),\r\n                                      'scale_candidates':ordered_scales,\r\n                                      'selection':'smallest denominator passing geometry, title and collision checks'}\r\n    for scale in ordered_scales:\r\n        trial={'scale':scale,'status':'no_fit','marker_profiles_tested':0,\r\n               'candidate_trials':[]}\r\n        best=None;best_score=None\r\n        # First try the ordinary region. For 1:25 only, a second pass can use\r\n        # the space above actual fixed footer notes that the generic reserved\r\n        # fraction excluded; fixed obstacles/printed bounds are NEVER disabled.\r\n        # Always try the original v6.14 strict solver first. ONLY 1:25 with\r\n        # original markers receives a second layout-footprint calculation that\r\n        # measures printable model + actual marker/annotation graphics + titles.\r\n        regions=[('standard','viewport',available)]\r\n        if (scale==25 and cfg.get('allow_compact_footer_retry_at_25',True)):\r\n            compact_cfg=dict(cfg)\r\n            compact_cfg['reserved_bottom_fraction']=float(\r\n                cfg.get('compact_footer_fraction_at_25',0.075))\r\n            if not (.04<=compact_cfg['reserved_bottom_fraction']<float(cfg['reserved_bottom_fraction'])):\r\n                raise ValueError('Compact footer fraction must be smaller than standard, and >=.04')\r\n            compact=safe_area(sheet,compact_cfg)\r\n            if compact.y0<available.y0-mm_to_ft(.1):\r\n                regions.append(('compact_footer','viewport',compact))\r\n        if (scale==25 and cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='original_direct_mirror'\r\n                and cfg.get('enable_25_content_footprints',True)):\r\n            regions.append(('standard_content','visible_content',available))\r\n            if scale==25 and cfg.get('allow_compact_footer_retry_at_25',True):\r\n                if 'compact' in locals() and compact.y0<available.y0-mm_to_ft(.1):\r\n                    regions.append(('compact_footer_content','visible_content',compact))\r\n        if (scale==25 and cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='original_direct_mirror'\r\n                and cfg.get('enable_25_sparse_parts',True)):\r\n            # Fixed sheet objects remain in the collision list. 'available' is\r\n            # NOT used as a hard height limit for sparse placement.\r\n            regions.append(('sparse_printed_parts','sparse_content',available))\r\n        trial['regions_tried']=[{'region':name,'footprint_basis':basis} for name,basis,_ in regions]\r\n        for region_name,basis,region in regions:\r\n            trial_cfg=dict(cfg)\r\n            trial_cfg['_layout_footprint_basis']=basis\r\n            if cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='original_direct_mirror':\r\n                profiles=[{'name':'original_marker_label_%smm'%gap,\r\n                           'height_ratio':1.0,'label_gap_mm':float(gap)}\r\n                          for gap in cfg.get('search_label_gap_mm',[5.,3.,2.])]\r\n            else:\r\n                profiles=marker_search_profiles(cfg,preferred=True)\r\n            for profile in profiles:\r\n                candidate=evaluate_profile(sheet,targets,records,geometry,region,fixed_with_bom,bom_limit,\r\n                                           trial_cfg,scale,profile)\r\n                candidate['usable_region_kind']=region_name\r\n                candidate['layout_footprint_basis']=basis\r\n                trial['marker_profiles_tested']+=1\r\n                compact={k:v for k,v in candidate.items() if k in (\r\n                    'profile','vertical_height_ratio','label_gap_mm','status','plan_footprint_after_mm',\r\n                    'saved_plan_height_mm','saved_plan_width_mm',\r\n                    'height_feasibility','plan_viewport_box_after_mm',\r\n                    'plan_label_extra_height_mm','title_reanchor_mm','geometry_elevation_title_realign','reason','layout',\r\n                    'plan_marker_proximity_diagnostics','hidden_x_adjustment',\r\n                    'usable_region_kind','layout_footprint_basis')}\r\n                trial['candidate_trials'].append(compact)\r\n                if candidate['status']!='error':\r\n                    shortfall=candidate.get('height_feasibility',{}).get('row_height_shortfall_mm',1e6)\r\n                    box=candidate.get('plan_footprint_after_mm',[1e6,1e6])\r\n                    score=(float(shortfall),float(box[1]),float(box[0]))\r\n                    if best is None or score<best_score:\r\n                        best=candidate;best_score=score\r\n                if candidate['status']=='fit':\r\n                    winning={'scale':scale,'profile':profile,'candidate':candidate,\r\n                             'region':region,'region_name':region_name,\r\n                             'layout_footprint_basis':basis}\r\n                    break\r\n            if winning is not None:\r\n                break\r\n        if winning is not None:\r\n            trial.update({k:v for k,v in winning['candidate'].items()\r\n                          if k not in ('profile',)})\r\n            trial['status']='fit'\r\n            trial['selected_region']=winning['region_name']\r\n            trial['selected_layout_footprint_basis']=winning['layout_footprint_basis']\r\n        else:\r\n            if best is not None:\r\n                trial.update({k:v for k,v in best.items()\r\n                              if k in ('plan_footprint_before_mm',\r\n                                       'plan_footprint_after_mm',\r\n                                       'saved_plan_height_mm','saved_plan_width_mm',\r\n                                       'reference_diagnostics',\r\n                                       'marker_visibility_other_views',\r\n                                       'height_feasibility','title_reanchor_mm',\r\n                                       'plan_title_outline_mm')})\r\n                trial['best_failed_profile']=best['profile']\r\n                trial['reason']='No layout fit among %d profile(s); best profile: %s (%s)' % (\r\n                    trial['marker_profiles_tested'],best['profile'],best.get('reason','no fit'))\r\n            else:\r\n                trial['status']='error'\r\n                trial['reason']='Every marker profile raised an error; see candidate_trials'\r\n        result['scale_trials'].append(trial)\r\n        if winning is not None:break\r\n    if winning is None:\r\n        result['scale_25_diagnostics']=next((x for x in result['scale_trials'] if x['scale']==25),None)\r\n        result['status']='no_fit'\r\n        result['error']='No tested marker positions or scales produced a collision-free layout. See candidate_trials and height_feasibility.'\r\n        return result\r\n    chosen=winning['scale']\r\n    winning_candidate=winning['candidate']\r\n    # The candidate loop already chose the LARGEST feasible printed drawing,\r\n    # never committing a scale which failed the actual sheet/layout trials.\r\n    result['scale_selection_reason']=('Selected 1:%d as the largest candidate scale '\r\n                                      '(smallest denominator) passing all live Revit '\r\n                                      'marker, title and layout checks.'%chosen)\r\n    result['selected_scale']=chosen\r\n    result['sparse_25_trial_used']=winning['layout_footprint_basis']=='sparse_content'\r\n    result['selected_sheet_region_mode']=winning['region_name']\r\n    result['selected_layout_footprint_basis']=winning['layout_footprint_basis']\r\n    result['accepted_usable_sheet_region_mm']=winning['region'].as_mm()\r\n    result['selected_gap_mm']=winning_candidate['layout']['gap_mm']\r\n    result['selected_label_gap_mm']=winning['profile']['label_gap_mm']\r\n    result['selected_marker_profile']=winning['profile']\r\n    result['reference_preview']=winning_candidate['reference_diagnostics']\r\n    result['original_marker_proximity_preview']=winning_candidate.get('plan_marker_proximity_diagnostics')\r\n    result['elevation_left_hidden_x_preview']=winning_candidate.get('hidden_x_adjustment')\r\n    if result['elevation_left_hidden_x_preview'] and result['elevation_left_hidden_x_preview'].get('status','').startswith('skipped'):\r\n        result['warnings'].append('Elevation Left X marker was not adjusted: %s'%\r\n                                  result['elevation_left_hidden_x_preview'].get('status'))\r\n    if cfg.get('original_marker_proximity',True) and cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='original_direct_mirror':\r\n        result['warnings'].append('Original section cut planes moved toward Plan Detail model and view crop widths may be reduced; verify both Elevation views and their symbols. No marker recreation.')\r\n    result['marker_strategy']=cfg.get('marker_strategy')\r\n    if cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='original_direct_mirror':\r\n        result['warnings'].append('Direct mirroring ORIGINAL Elevation Front markers changes source Elevation view origin/crop in prior Revit tests. Inspect geometry after apply. No markers created or hidden.')\r\n    if cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='reference_recreation_v613' and cfg.get('marker_placement_mode')=='geometry_proximity':\r\n        result['warnings'].append('SCHEMATIC REFERENCE MARKERS: placed near Plan Detail geometry rather than at the original source cut planes; source views and crops unchanged. Check whether this presentation is appropriate for your drawing.')\r\n    facing_conflicts=([r['name'] for r in result['reference_preview']\r\n                      if r.get('facing_reversed_vs_source')]\r\n                      if cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='reference_recreation_v613' else [])\r\n    result['reversed_facing_references']=facing_conflicts\r\n    if facing_conflicts:\r\n        result['warnings'].append('Initial head/tail facing diagnostic for %s; the Elevation Front reference '\r\n                                  'is mirrored after creation. Verify actual rendered orientation.' % ', '.join(facing_conflicts))\r\n    result['marker_visibility_other_views']=winning_candidate['marker_visibility_other_views']\r\n    result['layout_preview']=winning_candidate['layout']\r\n    result['geometry_title_alignment_preview']=winning_candidate.get('geometry_elevation_title_realign',{})\r\n    if 25 in ordered_scales and chosen!=25:\r\n        rejected25=next((x for x in result['scale_trials'] if x['scale']==25),None)\r\n        result['scale_25_diagnostics']={\r\n            'original_markers_can_inflate_viewport_bounds':cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='original_direct_mirror',\r\n            'status':'not_fit',\r\n            'reason':None if rejected25 is None else rejected25.get('reason'),\r\n            'candidate_reason_by_mode':([] if rejected25 is None else [\r\n                {'region':t.get('usable_region_kind'), 'basis':t.get('layout_footprint_basis'),\r\n                 'status':t.get('status'), 'reason':t.get('reason')}\r\n                for t in rejected25.get('candidate_trials',[])]),\r\n            'first_trial_reasons':([] if rejected25 is None else [\r\n                {'region':t.get('usable_region_kind'),\r\n                 'profile':t.get('profile'), 'footprint_basis':t.get('layout_footprint_basis'), 'status':t.get('status'),\r\n                 'reason':t.get('reason'),\r\n                 'height_feasibility':t.get('height_feasibility')}\r\n                for t in rejected25.get('candidate_trials',[])[:6]])}\r\n        result['warnings'].append('1:25 was tested but did not meet actual Revit safety/layout constraints. '\r\n                                  'See scale_25_diagnostics. No forced overflow was used.')\r\n    if chosen!=int(cfg['preferred_scale']):\r\n        result['warnings'].append('Adaptive scale selected 1:%s instead of nominal 1:%s' % (chosen,cfg['preferred_scale']))\r\n    if dry_run:\r\n        result['status']='preview_fit_with_orientation_warning' if facing_conflicts else 'preview_fit_uncommitted'\r\n        return result\r\n    # Preview already tried direct original mirroring, title alignment and full\r\n    # layout IN ROLLBACK transactions. Apply only on explicit user request.\r\n    # Keep layout-fit and transaction/rollback requirements to avoid partial edits.\r\n    selected_cfg=profile_configuration(cfg,winning['profile'])\r\n    selected_cfg['_layout_footprint_basis']=winning['layout_footprint_basis']\r\n    selected_records=[]\r\n    for record,item in zip(records,selected_cfg['references']):\r\n        data=dict(record);data['item']=item;selected_records.append(data)\r\n    apply_tx=Transaction(DOC,'APPLY v6.18.2 hidden X section + original markers + sparse layout')\r\n    apply_tx.Start()\r\n    try:\r\n        apply_scale(targets,chosen,selected_cfg)\r\n        result['final_elevation_left_hidden_x']=try_elevation_left_x_with_subtransaction(\r\n            targets,selected_cfg,chosen,baseline_plan_ids=model_ids)\r\n        new_bounds,new_model_ids=model_bounds(plan,selected_cfg)\r\n        if not set(model_ids).issubset(set(new_model_ids)):\r\n            raise ValueError('Moving Plan Detail X cut lost previously visible model IDs; abort')\r\n        created=perform_marker_strategy(plan,selected_records,new_bounds,selected_cfg,chosen)\r\n        if selected_cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='original_direct_mirror':\r\n            other_report={key:{'found':[],'hidden_in_this_trial':False}\r\n                          for key in ('front','left','iso')}\r\n        else:\r\n            other_report=other_view_marker_visibility(targets,selected_cfg)\r\n        result['final_title_diagnostics']=reanchor_titles_integrated(targets,selected_cfg)\r\n        if not selected_cfg.get('hide_markers_outside_plan',True) and any(\r\n                other_report[k]['found'] for k in ('front','left','iso')):\r\n            raise ValueError('Markers outside Plan Detail remain visible')\r\n        # Re-use the EXACT safe region accepted during the successful trial,\r\n        # including any compact-footer retry. Do not change collision policy.\r\n        solution,reason=check_layout(targets,winning['region'],fixed_with_bom,\r\n                                     selected_cfg,bom_limit,get_sheet_rect(sheet))\r\n        if solution is None:\r\n            raise ValueError('Final layout did not pass: '+str(reason))\r\n        if selected_cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='original_direct_mirror':\r\n            for rec in selected_records:\r\n                marker=DOC.GetElement(rec['original'].Id)\r\n                source=DOC.GetElement(rec['source'].Id)\r\n                if (marker is None or source is None or\r\n                        marker.IsHidden(plan) or\r\n                        elem_num(marker)!=elem_num(rec['original']) or\r\n                        elem_num(source)!=elem_num(rec['source'])):\r\n                    raise ValueError('Original source/marker changed ID or visibility after layout: %s'%rec['name'])\r\n            result['final_geometry_title_realign']={\r\n                key:raw_outline(vp.GetLabelOutline()).as_mm()\r\n                for key,(vp,v) in targets.items()\r\n                if raw_outline(vp.GetLabelOutline()) is not None}\r\n        result['final_reference_diagnostics']=created\r\n        result['final_marker_proximity']=next((d.get('plan_original_marker_envelope') for d in created\r\n                                               if d.get('plan_original_marker_envelope') is not None),None)\r\n        result['final_title_alignment']=solution.get('geometry_title_alignment_after_placement',{})\r\n        status=apply_tx.Commit()\r\n        if status!=TransactionStatus.Committed:\r\n            raise ValueError('Commit status was not Committed: '+str(status))\r\n        result['marker_visibility_other_views']=other_report\r\n        result['layout_preview']=solution\r\n        result['committed']=True\r\n        result['status']='applied_original_marker_mirror_layout_requires_visual_QA' if selected_cfg.get('marker_strategy')=='original_direct_mirror' else 'applied_reference_recreation_requires_visual_QA'\r\n    except Exception as exc:\r\n        result['error']=str(exc)[:900]\r\n        try:\r\n            tx_status=apply_tx.GetStatus()\r\n            if tx_status==TransactionStatus.Started:\r\n                rolled=apply_tx.RollBack()\r\n                result['rolled_back']=(rolled==TransactionStatus.RolledBack)\r\n                result['status']='rolled_back_apply_error' if result['rolled_back'] else 'rollback_not_confirmed'\r\n            elif tx_status==TransactionStatus.RolledBack:\r\n                result['status']='rolled_back_apply_error'\r\n                result['rolled_back']=True\r\n            elif tx_status==TransactionStatus.Committed:\r\n                result['status']='post_commit_exception_changes_may_remain'\r\n                result['committed']=True\r\n            else:\r\n                result['status']='transaction_state_uncertain'\r\n        except Exception as e:\r\n            result['status']='rollback_not_confirmed'\r\n            result['warnings'].append('CRITICAL: final rollback failed: '+str(e))\r\n    return result\r\n\r\ntry:\r\n    sheet=UnwrapElement(IN[0]) if IN[0] is not None else DOC.ActiveView\r\nexcept NameError:\r\n    sheet=IN[0] if IN[0] is not None else DOC.ActiveView\r\nexcept Exception:\r\n    sheet=DOC.ActiveView\r\ntry:overrides=dict(IN[1]) if len(IN)>1 and IN[1] else {}\r\nexcept Exception:overrides={}\r\n# Safe default: IN[2]=None/True always PREVIEWS (all transactions roll back).\r\n# Set IN[2]=False ONLY on a disposable original-sheet backup to APPLY.\r\ndry_run = (len(IN)<3 or IN[2] is None or bool(IN[2]))\r\nconfig=dict(DEFAULTS)\r\nconfig.update(overrides)\r\n# Source and geometry verification always remain active; approval flags are not needed.\r\nconfig['require_matching_source_facing']=False\r\nconfig['allow_reversed_horizontal_preview']=True\r\nconfig['approve_reversed_horizontal_commit']=True\r\nconfig['approve_marker_orientation']=True\r\nconfig['approve_commit']=True\r\ntry:\r\n    if not isinstance(sheet,ViewSheet):\r\n        raise ValueError('IN[0] is not a sheet and Revit active view is not a sheet')\r\n    TransactionManager.Instance.ForceCloseTransaction()\r\n    OUT=[run_sheet(sheet,config,dry_run)] \r\nexcept Exception as err:\r\n    OUT=[{'status':'error','error':str(err)[:1200], \r\n          'advice':'Do not commit; inspect details and transaction state'}]\r\n",
      "Engine": "CPython3",
